{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation","id":1474648,"title":"Does Magic Require Explanation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-14T14:40:56-08:00","id":1474648,"title":"Does Magic Require Explanation?","content":"Hello Everyone, so after many years I'm finally running my first 2nd edition campaign (yay \\o/) and with it I'm having some difficulty thinking about some issues, to which I ask for help. <br /> <br /> My question is, in a nutshell, &quot;can mages (without Arcanum 5) say: I'm doing this 'cause it is magic and that's that&quot; ?<br /> <br /> Now, for an ellaborate analysis of the issue (I'll try to keep it as short as I can):<br /> <br /> <br /> Problem: <br /> <br /> Mage A, with life 4, wants to change his friend's body to produce electricity like an eel.<br /> <br /> Mage A has no knowledge of biology, medicine nor anything &quot;scientifically&quot; about how any of this work. <br /> <br /> Question: Should mage A's Arcanum + gnosis be penalized somehow?<br /> <br /> Argument 1: No. It is magic. <br /> <br /> Argument 2: No, it is magic and Arcanum gives some institive knowledge about this stuff. Besides, it *is* magic<br /> <br /> Argument 3: Yes. This is an alteration of a complex system, mage doesn't truly understand and may have consequences for the body. <br /> <br /> Solution 1: A prior test of, let's say intelligence + medicine / science, so that Mage A may show understanding of the issues<br /> <br /> Solution 2: Casting a Knowing Practice, to gain the true knowledge of what he should be doing AND cast the changing spell under this spell influence. <br /> <br /> Variations:<br /> <br /> Mage A wants to create new functional limbs (arms or even wings: I think this could be a lesser penalization cause it is not that drastic)<br /> <br /> Mage B, with Matter 4, that wants to build a Gun, or a Car (fully out o magic), without no knowledge of science, mechanics, or even Cars in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> At first, Argument 3 does appeal to me, however, I soon realized I would have treated my mages unfairly, for different Arcana. <br /> <br /> Case: <br /> <br /> Mage C with Mind, reading thoughts or anything else. We have very little understanding of how thoughts and memories work and are stored/accessed inside the brain, and anything dealing with them, by the same metrics, should have a hard penalty.<br /> <br /> Mage D (even more difficult) with Time. any time effect seems to end my arguments that magic should have explanations of be reasonable somehow. Even if time itself my have some resistance to being changed, it doesnt truly enters in the question of *how* it is being done. It is just magic. <br /> <br /> <br /> Exception:<br /> <br /> I had came to the understanding that by having Arcanum 5, the Making practice just doesn't care about this stuff. So you can pretty much make stuff as you go without concerns about how anything is truly working: it just came to exist in that way. (like many software and their code I guess :P), so I would never penalize a 5 Making practice to do the same effects, these mages are trying to do with 1-4 dots. <br /> <br /> <br /> However, none of this helps me answer the problems of Mind and Time magic when it comes to penalizing or not acts of magic, and as I said I really do not want to treat players unfairly, nor to nerf them, but my mind just break at the idea that Mage A could do that to a human body without any penalty. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, could anyone try to help me with that?<br /> (and not in a: &quot;do what you feel&quot; kinda way, cause I'm conflicted, and players by default are against penalties :P). <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T15:12:22-08:00","id":1474654,"title":"","content":"Argument 1 is correct - it's magic.<br /> <br /> Knowledge of Phenomenal science benefits spellcasting by giving you a symbolset to leverage for bonuses, and lack thereof offers one way the ST can angle the spell going wrong in the event of Paradox, but spellcasting relies on your ability to conceptualize the <i>end result</i>.<br /> <br /> Penalties come from more intensive spell factors being harder to balance and <i>maybe</i> things that would normally mess with your ability to concentrate, but if a spell is producing an outcome, it produces the outcome \u2014 stuff like Shaping requires rolls because the spell makes the material shapable, but Transform Life gives a dog wings because magic was used to give it wings, and magic cast with mnemonic aids happens to be more likely to succeed even if you can also reach that outcome with no explanation or visible activity whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-14-2022, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T15:22:37-08:00","id":1474655,"title":"","content":"Argument 2. If Awakening wanted you to have to have dots in Science or Medicine to do Life effects, it would have including them in the default casting pool. Having knowledge of the Fallen World's rules to better use your magic is expressed through Rotes, and things like the Techne Merit.<br /> <br /> It's also worth considering that Transform Life's primary factor is Potency,not Duration. So if you want it to last more than a turn, you're going to be taking penalties and/or spending Reach as it is. It's not a lasting spell. It might not be the penalties you're thinking of, but it's worth keeping in mind that just because a mage can, in theory, perform this feat with no knowledge of the science involved thanks to their understanding of the pure supernal truths of how life really works, doesn't mean that it's easy for them to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T16:40:42-08:00","id":1474660,"title":"","content":"For the life of me, I can't find the post where Dave says it, but there was a post of his where he described it like &quot;a mage flies because the dream of flying is more powerful than gravity&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> Which is a fancy way of saying &quot;it happens because magic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T17:08:11-08:00","id":1474663,"title":"","content":"I find it easier to think like this from a \u2018crunchier\u2019 perspective: Spellcasting is already an Attribute + Skill roll, just like most other rolls are. It\u2019s just that the Attribute here is Gnosis, and the Skill here is the Arcanum used.<br /> <br /> So, just as you wouldn\u2019t need to add Crafts to a Dexterity + Medicine roll to do simple surgeries just because the surgery involves fine tools, you wouldn\u2019t need to add Medicine to a Gnosis + Life roll to do shapeshifting just because the healing involves biochemical reactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T17:58:01-08:00","id":1474667,"title":"","content":"In-character, mages have ways of explaining how their spells work to an extent, but they're often in philosophical and metaphysical terms, because everything that happens around gaining and using magic suggests to them that those are a more genuine form of reality than physical phenomena.<br /> <br /> So a mage has understanding of the nature of their target and the features they want to change, but not in terms of scientific biological knowledge.<br /> <br /> In the system that's encompassed by the Gnosis trait, a combination of reason, observation and intuition from which a mage is able to assemble the symbolic underpinnings of the world that they use to make the visual images of spells.<br /> <br /> To use a simple reference, a Matter spell to change a cube into a sphere isn't based on knowing and changing molecular arrangements, it's based on viewing roundness as a property of a subject and knowing how to give something more of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T10:39:49-08:00","id":1474744,"title":"","content":"My interpretation: If the mage has Life 4 they must understand the symbols required to cast those kinds of spells. The process of learning about it via mundane or arcane experience would have prepared them to create this kind of magic<br /> <br /> Out of game: it is an abstraction to allow fun things. So yes, it is just magic<br /> <br /> EDIT: The only ingame mechanical limitations are on spells like teleportation, if you don't have a spatial sympathy to a place to can't just imaging the outcome of the spell (even if you do have mundane knowledge, like where the whitehouse front lawn is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-15-2022, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T11:29:28-08:00","id":1474747,"title":"","content":"I'd like to thank everyone so far for their input, it did clarify things for me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T15:28:59-08:00","id":1474761,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that magic is all about supernal symbols, so when a Mage uses Life to remove a disease he isn't searching through the target's body for bacteria or viruses, he is looking through their supernal pattern for the supernal symbol of disease and then removing that. If he uses magic to make someone fly his isn't constructing the necessary bone and musculature for flight, he is adding the supernal symbol for flight to their pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T06:14:12-08:00","id":1474803,"title":"","content":"This meta of magic can be very hard to clear up. In some (mage the ascension, but the idea stands) editions, correspondence was basically always teleporting, occasionally coincidental if nobody watched you doing it and you could justify getting to the place somehow (it could be said that it was vulgar without witnesses, but that's the old debate). In other editions, you could use correspondence coincidentally to get a plane ticket to your destination. <br /> <br /> So, if a mage uses correspondence, would a plane ticket just materialize? Would a seat show up open, would the company be hacked? Would a plane be conjured from nothing if no flight was available to the destination? Or would you have Matter to make the ticket, then hack the company with Forces + correspondence, etc? Yes, it is magic, but how finely do you define 'magic'? Could I grow wings to fly using correspondence?<br /> <br /> It helps a lot to have everybody in the same general mind, but it is very easy to be both too restrictive and unfair. Try to be as lenient as possible with the players, but know that they will try to abuse the game if you do it too much. Accept that you will fail sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T12:22:09-08:00","id":1474817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474803#post1474803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This meta of magic can be very hard to clear up. In some (mage the ascension, but the idea stands) editions, correspondence was basically always teleporting, occasionally coincidental if nobody watched you doing it and you could justify getting to the place somehow (it could be said that it was vulgar without witnesses, but that's the old debate). In other editions, you could use correspondence coincidentally to get a plane ticket to your destination.<br /> <br /> So, if a mage uses correspondence, would a plane ticket just materialize? Would a seat show up open, would the company be hacked? Would a plane be conjured from nothing if no flight was available to the destination? Or would you have Matter to make the ticket, then hack the company with Forces + correspondence, etc? Yes, it is magic, but how finely do you define 'magic'? Could I grow wings to fly using correspondence?<br /> <br /> It helps a lot to have everybody in the same general mind, but it is very easy to be both too restrictive and unfair. Try to be as lenient as possible with the players, but know that they will try to abuse the game if you do it too much. Accept that you will fail sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would allow it only for flavor purposes, especially if the mages don't have a reason to be discrete with their casting. Lets say a feather was used as a yantra for teleportation, the target could get wings that they flap once to arrive at the destination. Should they use a satellite picture for remote casting, they could be digitized and sent through the screen to the location. Should they tear an old train ticket, then a plane hatch materialized before them, opens and pulls moves past them to teleport. Should they be casting a scrying spell by burning cigarettes (a discrete symbolic reference to Agni as the divine conveyor of information), I would allow them to burn and use the magical ash to circle the limits of the scrying window. If they use a scrying pool or lake, a drop of water could float up from it and grow into the scrying window. But any use beyond that would require the applicable Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T12:34:33-08:00","id":1474820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474803#post1474803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This meta of magic can be very hard to clear up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Awakening doesn't have Ascension's problems with how things work. There is, as there is in any highly flexible system like this, areas of interpretation. But the fact that Awakening is not a subjective consensual reality, and magic doesn't work by imposing personal belief over the current consensus-state, means none of the weird RBD stuff from early Ascension has any bearing on understanding Awakening (beyond things Awakening changed specifically to avoid that sort of debate). It should be noted that most of what you're talking about has been firmly addressed in Ascension by this point as well. M20 is abundantly clear that Correspondence can't summon a plane ticket as the &quot;effect&quot; of moving you from A to B.<br /> <br /> Space doesn't create a taxi out of thin air to transport you more quickly from A to B. There is no Practice that, when applied to Space, can have that result. The most you could do with Space is summon an existing taxi to where you are, but at that point you could have just teleported yourself to where you want to go.<br /> <br /> Awakening 2e doesn't have an RBD vs PBD debate. It's a PBD system. It doesn't have a HAP vs HOP debate, because there is no coincidental vs. vulgar w/o witnesses consideration. It only matters if you magic is obvious to actual witnesses or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T01:20:51-08:00","id":1474839,"title":"","content":"It's funny, with the way that the Supernal works, there is technically a level of power at which your desire to have a taxi consists of the universe being rewritten for a taxi to have always been there. It's just a bit beyond what really comes up in play, and is a tad overkill.<br /> <br /> But I do think that gets to a point that understanding the process of spells as altering Platonic Forms can help one grasp the idea that Awakened magic is usually very direct and elemental in what it does. Manipulation of the fundamentals doesn't readily lend itself to something like causing liars to spew beetles.<br /> <br /> One other thing I regard as a neat way to think about the magic is that it ought to function rationally, but doesn't have to. My interpretation of still using the term Paradox along with the newer rules is that Reaching beyond what is safe entails forming an imago that is messy and shaky, that does not constitute a fully coherent Supernal explanation of how the effect comes about. It still takes place, but it's that irrationality which provides an entry point for the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T08:56:49-08:00","id":1474904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474820#post1474820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Space doesn't create a taxi out of thin air to transport you more quickly from A to B. There is no Practice that, when applied to Space, can have that result. The most you could do with Space is summon an existing taxi to where you are, but at that point you could have just teleported yourself to where you want to go.<br /> <br /> Awakening 2e doesn't have an RBD vs PBD debate. It's a PBD system. It doesn't have a HAP vs HOP debate, because there is no coincidental vs. vulgar w/o witnesses consideration. It only matters if you magic is obvious to actual witnesses or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that it has points if you look finely enough.<br /> <br /> We all could agree that you can use life without medicine to heal or create an animal and that the animal would not 'look weird' for a veterinarian. Right? But if you use matter to, say, create a projector, without any technical knowledge, one could argue that it follows that you could - it follows your intention of having a projector. What would a projector technician see when fixing the projector afterward - a normal, technically correct projector with the correct serial numbers? Or would we have to a 'technology' sphere to do what life could?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T09:49:20-08:00","id":1474907,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474904#post1474904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you use matter to, say, create a projector, without any technical knowledge, one could argue that it follows that you could - it follows your intention of having a projector. What would a projector technician see when fixing the projector afterward - a normal, technically correct projector with the correct serial numbers? Or would we have to a 'technology' sphere to do what life could?</div> </div> </div> </div> That \u201cSphere\u201d would be Matter. If you want a material thing, it\u2019s Matter Patterning or Matter Making if there is no air. No construction knowledge required. And yeah, it\u2019d be a completely normal projector, since it\u2019s a shadow of the Ideal Projector projected onto the Fallen. It\u2019d have serial numbers unless you wanted it not to, since it would be odd for a projector not to have serial numbers, and it\u2019s working from the basis of the ideal.<br /> Literally the only knowledge required is to know a symbol for projector, like a mental image of one or just the word for projector, and the Matter Arcana knowledge required to Pattern or Make. The Supernal takes care of the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T13:15:13-08:00","id":1474921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474904#post1474904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that it has points if you look finely enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say you're doing an exercise in confirmation bias at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We all could agree that you can use life without medicine to heal or create an animal and that the animal would not 'look weird' for a veterinarian. Right? </div> </div> </div>No. It would fall within the normal parameters for that animal. Unless the vet is actively watching the process or the magic later provokes Dissonance, there's nothing for a Sleeper to notice. Even if there are any minor hints, the Quiescence would come into play.<br /> <br /> If a vet examines a cat on day 1, the cat is injured and completely healed by a mage on day 2, and examined by the vet again on day 3? The vet wouldn't notice anything amiss.<br /> <br /> If a mage creates a cat, and then takes it to the vet the next day, the cat would appear to be a normal cat. Even if the mage made sure the cat is the model of health, has a beautiful and rare fur pattern, and is incredibly affectionate and sociable, those traits would be remarkable, but not &quot;weird&quot; in a sense of provoking any response other than, &quot;wow you have an amazing cat, I'm jealous.&quot; No magical complications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would a projector technician see when fixing the projector afterward - a normal, technically correct projector with the correct serial numbers? </div> </div> </div>How does the technician know what the &quot;correct&quot; serial numbers are on a random projector? Correct implies either you're trying to duplicate an existing projector (which is a different spell from just creating one), but a successful duplication would include anything like a serial number, or you're trying to pass off the projector as one that's already part of a database of serial numbers... which would be a problem even if you weren't using magic to build a projector and then send it in for repairs.<br /> <br /> It would have appropriate serial numbers for the projector you're creating. Quiescence would kick in if those particular serial numbers don't match some database (those sorts of errors happen all the time, nothing magical about that), assuming the technician even bothers because you don't scan serial numbers when you're replacing parts on a projector... you just swap out the parts and get on with your day.<br /> <br /> Even if you're in a situation where checking the serial number would come up, and the serial number wouldn't match the specific set of them being consulted, the consequences would have to be incredibly contrived for it to be treated as anything other than a clerical error. And this would be no different than mundanely building the projector.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T21:50:11-08:00","id":1474945,"title":"","content":"One of the advantages of the general neo-platonic approach to magic is that, in opposition to Ascension where your imago needs to accomodate the entire way you understand a thing via the lens of your paradigm, you more or less just need the idea of the thing you're doing/creating/subverting/whatthefuckevering, and nature of reality between the Supernal and the Phenomenal/Fallen (however you go at understanding it) will fill in the blanks. All the things you do to affect your casting of a spell allows more control and more &quot;substantial reality&quot; to your &quot;idea&quot;, and if you fail to keep a grasp on your Reach, Paradox fills in some of the blank-<br /> <br /> But again, you don't even need to understand how pressure differentials created by the velocity of air going over a wing shape throws a plane into the air, because a mage's dream of flying is stronger than physics. If you need a cat, you don't need to know how a cat's urinary and digestive tract work, or even, strictly, that a cat needs to poop and pee, any more than you need to know the role of cat in Ancient Egyptian religions or the psychological effect of relationships between cats and humans as it relates to each side of the party.<br /> <br /> You need the idea of a cat, and you need to keep that manifestation away from the non-idea of a cat, and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T03:02:26-08:00","id":1474956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474945#post1474945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You need the idea of a cat, and you need to keep that manifestation away from the non-idea of a cat, and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or to put it another way, you need to know the supernal symbols relevant to cat-li-ness, which i assume is required Arcane/mundane experience learned from doing things like Knowing spells, investigating mysteries relating to Life, exploring the idea space exposed by the lower levels of the Life Arcanum. <br /> <br /> I mean, if all you have access to at first is Knowing, Unveiling, and Compelling, you can see the symbols as they already exist, and manipulate them into doing the things that they naturally do. <br /> <br /> 1 dot in any Arcanum doesn't require a lot of these deeper questions, because you simply see the world as it is, and poke it a little. But doing so opens up the possibility of higher practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-19-2022, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T03:46:22-08:00","id":1474958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474956#post1474956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or to put it another way, you need to know the supernal symbols relevant to cat-li-ness, which i assume is required Arcane/mundane experience learned from doing things like Knowing spells, investigating mysteries relating to Life, exploring the idea space exposed by the lower levels of the Life Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. You need to know that cats exist, and that's literally all you need to manipulate the Supernal symbol of cats using the Arcana and the Practices you know.<br /> <br /> And seeing Supernal symbols is done with Mage Sight, not any spells.<br /> <br /> Quick edit: If you want an explanation as to how mages can use Supernal symbols they've never experienced before (in the form of those symbols rather than their mundane counterparts), it's because being a mage gives you the ability to translate your mundane knowledge into the corresponding symbols (and vice versa). Higher Arcana ratings means you can do so with higher proficiency (and achieve more astonishing results) but just being a mage gives you the base knowledge required, just like how all mages can understand High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-19-2022, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T03:51:13-08:00","id":1474959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474958#post1474958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all. You need to know that cats exist, and that's literally all you need to manipulate the Supernal symbol of cats using the Arcana and the Practices you know.<br /> <br /> And seeing Supernal symbols is done with Mage Sight, not any spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>That suggests you can't give animals the ability to generate electricity (like an electric eel), weaving, without the knowledge of electric eels, and how they do it.<br /> <br /> Which seems more like &quot;magic needing an explaination&quot; idea.<br /> <br /> Knowing spells give you &quot;direct awareness <br /> of Supernal truth&quot; - which is what i was referring to. But yes, mage sight is not a spell, thank you for correcting me. It is still acquired along with the first dot in the arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T04:03:01-08:00","id":1474960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474959#post1474959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That suggests you can't give animals the ability to generate electricity (like an electric eel), weaving, without the knowledge of electric eels, and how they do it.<br /> <br /> Which seems more like &amp;quot;magic needing an explaination&amp;quot; idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Someone who doesn't know that animals can generate electricity <i>would never attempt a spell that gives them a natural way of generating electricity</i>. That's the reason why a tiny smidge of mundane knowledge is required.<br /> But once you know it's possible, you absolutely don't need to know how it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T04:08:23-08:00","id":1474961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474960#post1474960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no. Someone who doesn't know that animals can generate electricity <i>would never attempt a spell that gives them a natural way of generating electricity</i>. That's the reason why a tiny smidge of mundane knowledge is required.<br /> But once you know it's possible, you absolutely don't need to know how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if someone tells you, or you read it in a book, then you can try it, and the spell just works. What if they are lying?<br /> <br /> Or just wrong (like how scientists thought spider's reactions are faster than possible - for a message to get to the brain and back - giving rise to spiderman's precognition like 'spidey sense' - when infact the spider has a 'brain' halfway along its leg so the journey is shorter)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T06:34:40-08:00","id":1474966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474961#post1474961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if someone tells you, or you read it in a book, then you can try it, and the spell just works. What if they are lying?<br /> <br /> Or just wrong (like how scientists thought spider's reactions are faster than possible - for a message to get to the brain and back - giving rise to spiderman's precognition like 'spidey sense' - when infact the spider has a 'brain' halfway along its leg so the journey is shorter)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what <i>exactly</i> are you trying to accomplish with the spell? To increase reaction times? To give someone the reaction times of a spider? Both of these are fully valid effects for a Life spell.<br /> The fact that you're mistaken about how spiders have so good reaction times doesn't matter unless you're specifically trying to replicate a spider's ability to send messages from their sensory organs to their brains impossibly fast. But that's honestly a stupid way to go about designing your spells, both out-of-setting and in-setting.<br /> <br /> Note that only spells that explicitly replicate pre-existing traits/objects/lifeforms/etc (like Transform Life) requires those to already exist. Most spells don't give a shit about such things, so you could cast other Life spells to give you traits that doesn't exist (with the drawback that each trait would be a separate spell). The only knowledge required for them is the knowledge required to come up with the idea of those spells in the first place. Without that idea you couldn't cast the spell because you literally haven't thought of that spell yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T07:03:15-08:00","id":1474967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474907#post1474907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That \u201cSphere\u201d would be Matter. If you want a material thing, it\u2019s Matter Patterning or Matter Making if there is no air. No construction knowledge required. And yeah, it\u2019d be a completely normal projector, since it\u2019s a shadow of the Ideal Projector projected onto the Fallen. It\u2019d have serial numbers unless you wanted it not to, since it would be odd for a projector not to have serial numbers, and it\u2019s working from the basis of the ideal.<br /> Literally the only knowledge required is to know a symbol for projector, like a mental image of one or just the word for projector, and the Matter Arcana knowledge required to Pattern or Make. The Supernal takes care of the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, could I make 'John's car keys', or nuclear device in the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","user":"pcontop","date":". 02-19-2022, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T07:27:27-08:00","id":1474973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474921#post1474921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say you're doing an exercise in confirmation bias at this point.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little close to a personal attack. Did I do something to grant that? My understanding of this topic is about the dissonance between the idealized reality of the mage spheres and the concrete real world. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> No. It would fall within the normal parameters for that animal. Unless the vet is actively watching the process or the magic later provokes Dissonance, there's nothing for a Sleeper to notice. Even if there are any minor hints, the Quiescence would come into play.<br /> <br /> If a vet examines a cat on day 1, the cat is injured and completely healed by a mage on day 2, and examined by the vet again on day 3? The vet wouldn't notice anything amiss.<br /> <br /> If a mage creates a cat, and then takes it to the vet the next day, the cat would appear to be a normal cat. Even if the mage made sure the cat is the model of health, has a beautiful and rare fur pattern, and is incredibly affectionate and sociable, those traits would be remarkable, but not &quot;weird&quot; in a sense of provoking any response other than, &quot;wow you have an amazing cat, I'm jealous.&quot; No magical complications.<br /> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less what I meant, by saying that a vet would not see issues. No organs in wrong places, etc. All the insides and outsides of the cat are not only functional, but within the understand and expectations of someone who has experience with the real thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> How does the technician know what the &quot;correct&quot; serial numbers are on a random projector? Correct implies either you're trying to duplicate an existing projector (which is a different spell from just creating one), but a successful duplication would include anything like a serial number, or you're trying to pass off the projector as one that's already part of a database of serial numbers... which would be a problem even if you weren't using magic to build a projector and then send it in for repairs.<br /> <br /> It would have appropriate serial numbers for the projector you're creating. Quiescence would kick in if those particular serial numbers don't match some database (those sorts of errors happen all the time, nothing magical about that), assuming the technician even bothers because you don't scan serial numbers when you're replacing parts on a projector... you just swap out the parts and get on with your day.<br /> <br /> Even if you're in a situation where checking the serial number would come up, and the serial number wouldn't match the specific set of them being consulted, the consequences would have to be incredibly contrived for it to be treated as anything other than a clerical error. And this would be no different than mundanely building the projector. </div> </div> </div>Well, how would a technician notice if the serial numbers are right or not depends on the technician's qualifications and conditions. Realistically, if he needs to fix the projector, he might need to check the labels on the parts to order new ones. He might be checking it up if the projector is still covered by the warranty. When some mage wants 'a projector', does he get a copy of a concrete projector that exists somewhere or an ideal platonic version of it with serial numbers that do not match any database? Will the quiescence go all the way to the database to make the company allow the warranty?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I'll make an ignorant question of MtAw: if quiescence hits at this late time, is it defined if the mage gets paradox then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T07:55:37-08:00","id":1474979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474973#post1474973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mage spheres</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcana, singular Arcanum. Spheres are Ascension's term.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and I'll make an ignorant question of MtAw: if quiescence hits at this late time, is it defined if the mage gets paradox then? </div> </div> </div>Paradox applies at the point of casting the spell; anything afterward is Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T09:35:58-08:00","id":1474982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474967#post1474967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, could I make 'John's car keys', or nuclear device in the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. As long as you have a symbol for whatever you want. That\u2019s the power of Patterning/Making. There is a Ruling spell called Shaping to make stuff from it\u2019s components without tools, and that one requires actual technical knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474973#post1474973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more or less what I meant, by saying that a vet would not see issues. No organs in wrong places, etc. All the insides and outsides of the cat are not only functional, but within the understand and expectations of someone who has experience with the real thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. We are working with the high end of regular Mage Magic. This is one of the perks. The only way for Paradox or Dissonance to occur is if someone wonders why there is suddenly now a normal cat running around, and there\u2019s enough easy explanations for that under most situations that there wouldn\u2019t be any problem unless you brought a cat into existence directly in front of someone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474967#post1474967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When some mage wants 'a projector', does he get a copy of a concrete projector that exists somewhere or an ideal platonic version of it with serial numbers that do not match any database?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. Depends on how the spell was made. Want a copy? You get a copy. Want a completely unique one? Don\u2019t expect it\u2019s serial numbers, if it has them, to match up to a data base. Just want a projector? The projector that comes out is a normal example of whatever projector you think of when you think projector\u2026probably with it\u2019s own unique serial number, since a normal projector doesn\u2019t completely match another. Technically none of the things made by the spell are actually the ideal though, just shadows of the ideal on the wall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474967#post1474967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the quiescence go all the way to the database to make the company allow the warranty?</div> </div> </div> </div> No. Unless you cast on the data base too. And that\u2019s probably a separate spell. Making a copy is probably the best option in this scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474967#post1474967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I'll make an ignorant question of MtAw: if quiescence hits at this late time, is it defined if the mage gets paradox then?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. They don\u2019t. If Magic is spotted by a sleeper after casting, they suffer a breaking point, and roll their Integrity. Depending on the Number of Successes, some or all of the spell gets eroded away. That\u2019s called Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-19-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:39:31-08:00","id":1474991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474956#post1474956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or to put it another way, you need to know the supernal symbols relevant to cat-li-ness, which i assume is required Arcane/mundane experience learned from doing things like Knowing spells, investigating mysteries relating to Life, exploring the idea space exposed by the lower levels of the Life Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even that level of investigation isn't really necessary for mages doing what is fairly rudimentary to the Practices of their Arcana.<br /> <br /> I think there are two key sections of the core that convey the basis for how mages know what to form their imagos out of. <br /> <br /> On page 66:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage casts spells by virtue of her Path \u2014 a massive, theoretically near-infinite set of magical symbols she can sense and understand. To cast a spell, she imagines the effect she desires, focuses her mind on the symbols of her Path that will create that effect (the Imago), and through the medium of her Gnosis makes the world obey. </div> </div> </div>So that establishes that access to the perception of those symbols is basically the definition of having a Path. I find the descriptions in Signs of Sorcery to help elaborate on that a bit; how the semiotics differ across Paths and what those contribute to its ultimate philosophy, while still having the idea that each one contains symbols that cover basically anything. An Acanthus sees the Matter Arcanum in terms of tools that serve the functions of pursuing destined results, a Mastigos in terms of end points to attachments and focuses of purpose or desire for thinking beings, an Obrimos as a firm foundation point from which action to be taken and channelled, but manipulation of all of those collections of symbols are sufficient to accomplish basically every spell of the Matter Arcanum.<br /> <br /> The other is in the description of Gnosis, from page 84:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gnosis is largely a subconscious awareness. It\u2019s your character\u2019s ability to take a mental leap beyond what others can; she can connect dots others cannot even see. She understands the universe intuitively, and can see the threads she must pull to enact meaningful change. </div> </div> </div>Followed by the descriptions of how that is experienced per Path. I find that to convey the idea that mages experience the basic sense of what symbols are associated with what subjects and will accomplish what results just from knowing them and thinking about what they want. In those terms, I would think that a lot of the time Mage Sight amounts to actually looking directly to find what it is they're actually engaging with while walking their Path and working their magic. It could be a bit like the difference between being a runner and having dissected leg muscles.<br /> <br /> I'd say that a lot of the time Knowing spells aren't really about seeing the symbols so much as knowing what the symbols translate into as the phenomenal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:54:58-08:00","id":1474994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474973#post1474973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I do something to grant that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep bringing Ascension stuff into an Awakening discussion, and are trying to backwards justify why this is legitimate. Awakening is Awakening. If you want to learn about Awakening, focus on asking about it, rather than assuming things from Ascension apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, how would a technician notice if the serial numbers are right or not depends on the technician's qualifications and conditions. </div> </div> </div>OK, I don't think you've ever done projector repair. I got saddled with AV repair as part of a high-school job that wasn't about that at all, because I was working for family friends and they knew I knew how to do these sorts of things.<br /> <br /> I never scanned anything that came from the projector itself. I look at labels, sure, to confirm the general model; not the specific unit. The specific unit doesn't matter, they're all the same. What I scanned were the internal company barcodes they slapped on everything so they could track where it was, and who had serviced it.<br /> <br /> There's no high level projector repair system. They're projectors.<br /> <br /> An example that much better deals with what you're talking about are cars. Cars have a VIN, VINs are placed in at least three different places on a car. Why? Because car theft (both whole and parts) is a profitable business. VINs are part of how cars are tracks to ensure they're not stolen, even if you take them apart and put them in other cars. VINs are required to be scanned even over relatively minor repairs by shops, just to cut down on car theft related crimes. So if you magic a car into existence, it will have a VIN (that's part of the ideal of &quot;car&quot;), but unless you do something about it, the VIN is going to be wrong, which is a big problem if it ever gets scanned (which is going to be necessary for things like keeping it licensed and registered).<br /> <br /> These sorts of bureaucratic hoops only exist if there's a reason for them to exist. For the vast majority of consumer products the serial number is probably never scanned after it leaves the factory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and I'll make an ignorant question of MtAw: if quiescence hits at this late time, is it defined if the mage gets paradox then? </div> </div> </div>Quiescence is simply the aspect of the Lie that causes normal humans to forget or rationalize magic, and assume mundane explanation, so that they don't question their reality. That's all. This is why Awakening only concerns itself with obvious magic: magic that challenges the Quiescence and until a person can't handle the conflict between what they know they're experiencing and what the Lie is telling them isn't real. As noted Paradox governs what happens in the moment of casting, and Dissonance covers what happens if a Sleeper sees obvious magic after casting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T05:09:47-08:00","id":1475029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474966#post1474966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, what <i>exactly</i> are you trying to accomplish with the spell? To increase reaction times? To give someone the reaction times of a spider? Both of these are fully valid effects for a Life spell.<br /> The fact that you're mistaken about how spiders have so good reaction times doesn't matter unless you're specifically trying to replicate a spider's ability to send messages from their sensory organs to their brains impossibly fast. But that's honestly a stupid way to go about designing your spells, both out-of-setting and in-setting.<br /> <br /> Note that only spells that explicitly replicate pre-existing traits/objects/lifeforms/etc (like Transform Life) requires those to already exist. Most spells don't give a shit about such things, so you could cast other Life spells to give you traits that doesn't exist (with the drawback that each trait would be a separate spell). The only knowledge required for them is the knowledge required to come up with the idea of those spells in the first place. Without that idea you couldn't cast the spell because you literally haven't thought of that spell yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to do anything, just think through the consequences of how magic is being described to work.<br /> <br /> If mage Tim hears that spiders can respond faster thanphysics/biology would allow, and decides to try and give this trait to his cabal mate, Jack the arrow. Attempting to give 'spidey sense' - which is <br /> <br /> &quot;a precognitive sixth sense referred to as his &quot;Spider-Sense,&quot; which alerts him to danger.[119]&quot; - according to wikipedia.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it should work likea time effect, but only for physical stimulus.<br /> <br /> Would it fail because the idea you had isn't Actually how spiders work. I.e. the supernal and the scientist who came up with this idea disagree. Or can you just make a precognition sense with Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T05:20:55-08:00","id":1475030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474991#post1474991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even that level of investigation isn't really necessary for mages doing what is fairly rudimentary to the Practices of their Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, i guess that answers most of my curiosity. <br /> <br /> Still studying mysteries which may grant beats will be helpful for raising Arcana ratings and Gnosis. So in the infinite symbology available to you, experience plays the role of getting a grasp on those things you already had access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T05:21:00-08:00","id":1475031,"title":"","content":"You need to be more specific. Here's four different ways to do what Tim wants to do:<br /> <br /> a.) Tim attempts to give Jack a spider's sense of precognition using the spell Transform Life.<br /> This would fail because spider's don't have a sense of precognition.<br /> <br /> b.) Tim attempts to give Jack precognition using only Life magic.<br /> This would fail because Life is incapable of granting precognition.<br /> <br /> c.) Tim attempts to give Jack a spider's increased reaction times using the spell Transform Life.<br /> This would work because spiders have increased reaction times and that trait can be replicated.<br /> <br /> d.) Tim attempts to give Jack increased reaction times using only Life magic.<br /> This would work because Life is capable of increasing reaction times as they're based on biological factors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T11:56:25-08:00","id":1475053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475029#post1475029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If mage Tim hears that spiders can respond faster thanphysics/biology would allow...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem with this premise, is that mages should basically all know that this is a bad starting point. There's no such thing as &quot;a biological organism that does something the rules of biology don't allow.&quot; That's not how the rules of the Fallen World work. Without access to the Supernal, creatures are bound by the rules of the world they exist in, so the idea that a naturally occurring animal can do things impossible for biological organisms to do just don't work. So either:<br /> <br /> 1) It's sensationalized/mythologized lay misconceptions about what science cannot explain, or has not explained yet.<br /> <br /> 2) It's something Quiescence or Quiescence-like where a supernatural effect was mistaken for a natural one and got twisted around into an odd science publication (likely starting #1 in the first place).<br /> <br /> Mages are not the kind of people that take Sleeper science at face value (they understand the true rules of the world far better than scientists can), and are going to be even more skeptical of all of the wild pop-culture science &quot;facts&quot; that happen because science reporting is rarely both good and interesting (and interesting usually beats good in terms of what makes non-scientific publication).<br /> <br /> Mages are Obsessed with Mysteries. That sort of inquisitive mentality leads to a great deal of skepticism for &quot;too good to be true&quot; claims. It might not count as a Mystery, but most mages would at least Google something like that to see that it's just one of those silly science pop-culture myths and not something real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T15:27:09-08:00","id":1475063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475053#post1475053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the problem with this premise, is that mages should basically all know that this is a bad starting point. There's no such thing as &amp;quot;a biological organism that does something the rules of biology don't allow.&amp;quot; That's not how the rules of the Fallen World work.<br /> <br /> <br /> most mages would at least Google something like that to see that it's just one of those silly science pop-culture myths and not something real.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the question in the thread is whether you need to know the technical side of how the real world works. <br /> <br /> Now your answer appears to rely on the Mage knowing everything about the real world.<br /> <br /> As for googling the answer, i was honestly thinking of a 1920s* character for whom that is not an option... Because as you say a modern mage likely knows better. Not all mage's from all period would. And the premise is just to test the limits of &quot;you just imagine the thing and it becomes real&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are lots of things a mage doesn't know about how the fallen world works, there are vampires and sin-eaters, there are werecreatures and cryptids. And there is no reasons for a Mage, in particular one who knows most of these things to be real, to not believe this is possible. Or at least be able to imagine it.<br /> <br /> <br /> *i don't know why i have the 20s in my mind for when this bad science originated, especially since Spiderman is much later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T15:31:41-08:00","id":1475064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475031#post1475031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a.) Tim attempts to give Jack a spider's sense of precognition using the spell Transform Life.<br /> This would fail because spider's don't have a sense of precognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, i thought i was being clear. This is my presumed answer, at which point does Tim know why it failed?<br /> <br /> Did he try to grasp the symbols and fail to form an Imago, and thus realised that it isn't actually possible (at least as described by the erroneous science)? <br /> <br /> Or does it just fail like any spellcasting roll and Tim may attempt it again later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T16:06:26-08:00","id":1475065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475063#post1475063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the question in the thread is whether you need to know the technical side of how the real world works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but, having an appropriate skeptical outlook about Sleeper science is not a &quot;need to know the technical side of how the real world works.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can see the Truth of the rules of how the world works, and I know how little Sleepers understand,&quot; is not technical knowledge, but it is knowledge pretty much every mage has,and as such should assumed to behave as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now your answer appears to rely on the Mage knowing everything about the real world. </div> </div> </div>Please justify this, because it is very far from a logical extrapolation from what I said.<br /> <br /> I said that mages shouldn't trust Sleeper science when it comes to outlandish claims because they know Sleeper science is a Fallen practice studying the rules of the Fallen World and lacks the benefit of access to the Supernal. This doesn't require any knowledge of any specific topic. It requires not trusting people's claims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for googling the answer, i was honestly thinking of a 1920s* character for whom that is not an option... </div> </div> </div>I have very little interest in this turning into a series of, &quot;but what about this more constrained scenario,&quot; goal post shifting.<br /> <br /> They're mages. Again. They are obsessed investigators of mysteries. They can just find out, even if it used to take a few minutes instead of a few seconds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the premise is just to test the limits of &quot;you just imagine the thing and it becomes real&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Why are you doing that? Mages don't just &quot;imagine&quot; the thing and &quot;it becomes real.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are lots of things a mage doesn't know about how the fallen world works, there are vampires and sin-eaters, there are werecreatures and cryptids. And there is no reasons for a Mage, in particular one who knows most of these things to be real, to not believe this is possible. Or at least be able to imagine it. </div> </div> </div>I phrased things they way I did to head this issue off already.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T16:59:40-08:00","id":1475066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475063#post1475063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for googling the answer, i was honestly thinking of a 1920s* character for whom that is not an option... Because as you say a modern mage likely knows better. Not all mage's from all period would. And the premise is just to test the limits of &quot;you just imagine the thing and it becomes real&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any mage in a position to be transposing qualities from one living being onto another has the ability to examine either of those beings.<br /> <br /> The spells for perceiving and messing with radio waves still work in eras preceding the invention of radio, and the long history of Awakened astronomer traditions and the general weirdness of the world mean there's no significant obstacle to mages knowing how to make use of them once they're clued in \u2014 and knowing that spiders aren't precognitive is, by comparison, very easy for characters whose awareness of the animal kingdom includes instinctive reactions and heightened mundane senses.<br /> <br /> Simply put, mages are a little more likely than the average person to put together that &quot;spider sense&quot; is the early warning system known as &quot;eyes,&quot; and at the level of difference in reaction time you're talking about, it's still more sensible for those characters to try and transpose &quot;whatever quality gives spiders that reaction speed&quot; than a hypothetical supernatural ability using a Gross Arcanum. Whether you bolster the spell with symbols of foresight or symbols of speed or quick thinking may steer the way the spell can go wrong if Paradox strikes, but the end result is not going to provide a quality that doesn't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-20-2022, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T18:10:31-08:00","id":1475069,"title":"","content":"A hopefully useful example:<br /> <br /> A Neolithic Obrimos using Forces with their Mage Sight is going to see and grok the gist of nuclear radiation. They may not be able to explain it like a modern physicist does, but they still get it at a time where most people aren't even in a position to really qualify it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T18:15:48-08:00","id":1475070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have very little interest in this turning into a series of, &quot;but what about this more constrained scenario,&quot; goal post shifting </div> </div> </div>The scenario is relevant only in understanding the underlying principle. If i had picked an example of a Death effect which some vampire/sin-eaters had told them about it could he far more difficult to google.<br /> <br /> The idea is, if you can imagine something which isn't possible, what happens?<br /> <br /> Responding directly to this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1474958#post1474958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. You need to know that cats exist, and that's literally all you need</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying, but what if cats don't exist. Can you still Make a cat because some Cryptids hunter described it to you (which i think the answer is yes, because you are not limited to Making things which actually do exist, so bad example - but you can't make a cat with precognition).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any mage in a position to be transposing qualities from one living being onto another has the ability to examine either of those beings. </div> </div> </div>I think that was my original suggestion. This mage has experience examining beings by the time the have access to these practices. So they know how to manipulate the symbols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T18:48:52-08:00","id":1475074,"title":"","content":"So, this conversation is still going on?<br /> <br /> I think I can parse the matter in a simpler manner. I'm not sure, but I'll try.<br /> <br /> Mage the Ascension was about reality being ultimately defined by belief, and weird results could arise when conflicting beliefs clashed. This is <b><u>not</u></b> Ascension.<br /> <br /> Quite the contrary, Awakening has the same open-ended magic system built upon the opposite premise in-lore: reality has well defined natural rules and magic work upon them. It happens that science is ill suited to find its actual rules, while Mages have unfair advantages to do so.<br /> <br /> From there, it is the <i><u>setting's natural laws</u></i> that aren't necessarily as similar to RL as it seems at first glance, but that doesn't mean they are not as strict. They are <i>undefined from the player's perspective</i>, but that's it. At the end of the day, a Mage is as incapable as anyone of doing something actually impossible.<br /> <br /> Knowledge and Ability with technical details aren't required. Why? The same reason Chemistry, Electrodynamics and Cooking are distinct abilities through and through despite dealing with the exact same body of phenomena. Knowing all of them may give you new insights with what to do with them, but you don't need to know one to understand the other, neither becomes good at one by learning the other. A Chemist with deep knowledge of electrodynamics and no cooking experience will still be a terrible cook.<br /> <br /> At the end, a Mage with enough Life has enough knowledge of the &quot;Magical Science&quot; to: see and understand the Symbol for a spider's senses and reactions, to understand how this Symbol can be applied to a person, and what effects this will have from the standpoint of the Supernal Symbols. It works because it is possible, not just because the Mage wills it or imagines it (even if imagining is part of the process, just as putting your hands in the dough is part of the baking process). If the Mage tries the actually impossible, it fails because it is impossible, but the Mage's understanding of the result under other sciences, while valid, doesn't change if it will work or not.<br /> <br /> No penalty is necessary. To keep with the example, the magic works because its magic, but specifically in terms of the setting it works because the end result (a person with functional spider senses and no drawbacks) is what happens when the Symbol for the spider senses is correctly attached to the person without the addition of any drawback Symbols, and the natural laws of Supernal phenomena determine that the organism adapt in such and such ways to comply. The Mage needs not to know how it works under the laws of &quot;mundane&quot; Biology, but it does also work under the laws of mundane <b><u><i>CofD</i></u></b> Biology all the same. Indeed, a Mage with enough Biology knowledge could then seek to study the end result as a Mystery in itself, because the Mage knows enough of Biology to understand the peculiarities of the result from that perspective, that is still a valid one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T01:24:40-08:00","id":1475092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475074#post1475074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this conversation is still going on?<br /> <br /> I think I can parse the matter in a simpler manner. I'm not sure, but I'll try.<br /> <br /> Mage the Ascension was about reality being ultimately defined by belief, and weird results could arise when conflicting beliefs clashed. This is <b><u>not</u></b> Ascension.<br /> <br /> Quite the contrary, Awakening has the same open-ended magic system built upon the opposite premise in-lore: reality has well defined natural rules and magic work upon them. It happens that science is ill suited to find its actual rules, while Mages have unfair advantages to do so.<br /> <br /> From there, it is the <i><u>setting's natural laws</u></i> that aren't necessarily as similar to RL as it seems at first glance, but that doesn't mean they are not as strict. They are <i>undefined from the player's perspective</i>, but that's it. At the end of the day, a Mage is as incapable as anyone of doing something actually impossible.<br /> <br /> Knowledge and Ability with technical details aren't required. Why? The same reason Chemistry, Electrodynamics and Cooking are distinct abilities through and through despite dealing with the exact same body of phenomena. Knowing all of them may give you new insights with what to do with them, but you don't need to know one to understand the other, neither becomes good at one by learning the other. A Chemist with deep knowledge of electrodynamics and no cooking experience will still be a terrible cook.<br /> <br /> At the end, a Mage with enough Life has enough knowledge of the &amp;quot;Magical Science&amp;quot; to: see and understand the Symbol for a spider's senses and reactions, to understand how this Symbol can be applied to a person, and what effects this will have from the standpoint of the Supernal Symbols. It works because it is possible, not just because the Mage wills it or imagines it (even if imagining is part of the process, just as putting your hands in the dough is part of the baking process). If the Mage tries the actually impossible, it fails because it is impossible, but the Mage's understanding of the result under other sciences, while valid, doesn't change if it will work or not.<br /> <br /> No penalty is necessary. To keep with the example, the magic works because its magic, but specifically in terms of the setting it works because the end result (a person with functional spider senses and no drawbacks) is what happens when the Symbol for the spider senses is correctly attached to the person without the addition of any drawback Symbols, and the natural laws of Supernal phenomena determine that the organism adapt in such and such ways to comply. The Mage needs not to know how it works under the laws of &amp;quot;mundane&amp;quot; Biology, but it does also work under the laws of mundane <b><u><i>CofD</i></u></b> Biology all the same. Indeed, a Mage with enough Biology knowledge could then seek to study the end result as a Mystery in itself, because the Mage knows enough of Biology to understand the peculiarities of the result from that perspective, that is still a valid one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Thank you for the detailed reply.<br /> <br /> The only thing to add is 'a Mage with enough Life...' - without enough life some things will fail. Especially where that is 6+ dots required, a mage may think things are impossible. Or impossible for them.<br /> <br /> Would that 'feel' the same? You see and understand the symbols and realise you can't do a thing, perhaps because you are missing a symbol?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T02:37:57-08:00","id":1475094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475070#post1475070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is, if you can imagine something which isn't possible, what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Supernal Realms comprise the set of possible truths. Spellcasting is literally drawing these truths from the Supernal Realms and incarnating them in the world. Each Arcanum is literally a measure of your understanding of how to grasp and incarnate a subset of these possible truths, just like how Science is a measure of your understanding of how to leverage the laws of physics and mathematics.<br /> <br /> The set of impossibilities, things which not only are not true but cannot be true, is the Abyss. Another word for an impossible self-contradiction is a Paradox.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T08:03:57-08:00","id":1475105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475092#post1475092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing to add is 'a Mage with enough Life...' - without enough life some things will fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such failure is more akin to the failure due to lack of knowledge.<br /> <br /> The key here is that the Symbol must be understood and correctly manipulated and attached. A Mage without enough Life either can't grasp enough of the Symbol to be sure about the right one or to be sure how to attach them. The Arcana represent knowledge about a set of Symbols, including the knowledge needed to identify them. Perception is also learned, after all.<br /> <br /> Anyone can look at a rock that has crystals in it. Only a properly trained person can identify the minerals in that rock, perceive nuances and find the pieces that will shine if polished. To others it is just a dull rock and nothing can even be attempted except study it further. A trained person looks at a piece of meat and sees the telltale signs of where one cut becomes another, others just see a piece of meat and may at most have the impression that it seems odd. A blind person that undergoes some procedure to acquire vision can't tell apart a tree from a slab of concrete, they don't just can't name them, they literally can't tell them apart until they have enough experience. All of this is actual IRL facts about perception.<br /> <br /> Imagine now a blind person undergoing a procedure to acquire sight, then studying the minutiae of gem cutting and jewelry. That's a Mage in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> From this, the mechanical differences between Magic and other Abilities is merely a design choice. Each dot represent a greater gap in knowledge and understanding, but not an actual distinct process, at least not in a demonstrable way. It is just that making similar tables and rules for mundane Abilities won't have the same pay off for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T08:08:07-08:00","id":1475106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475092#post1475092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that 'feel' the same? You see and understand the symbols and realise you can't do a thing, perhaps because you are missing a symbol?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just speculation, but I'd imagine that for effects beyond their available Practices they would simply not know how to formulate the symbols to get the desired result. It's like having the dictionary of a language right in your head so you know what all individual words mean, but you don't know enough grammar to correctly put them in the right order. For an invalid spell I'd imagine it's more like being able to make a grammatically correct sentence but failing to convey anything meaningful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T12:14:26-08:00","id":1475136,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Magic also overrules whatever phenomena the symbols apply to, but nothing beyond that. Create Life is a classic example:</span></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage casts a Making</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Supernal:</b> Ok, he is creating a cat. Orange fur, stripes, fat, yep, got all those symbols. Now where is that last...aha, the eats lasagna property. Symbols assembled, ship the Imago.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Garfield appears.</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage casts another Making</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Supernal:</b> This time its a dragon, based on Ancalagon. Scale factor checks out. Fire breath via a flamethrower like mechanism, I think I can make it using a better version of the bombardier beetle's symbols. Armored hide, dense skeleton, easy. Razor fangs, sharp claws, leathery wings. Ok, all set, ship the Imago.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fallen World:</b> Hey, just a quick check. Did that Imago include any Forces symbols to overwrite the laws of physics ?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Supernal:</b> No....</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fallen World:</b> Well then...carry on</span></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dragon materializes </span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dragon:</b> <i>cough</i>...my bones collapsed on themselves, why, what is the Square-Cube Law ? My wings cannot fly, what are aerodynamics? EVERYTHING IS PAIN !!!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Understanding Fallen principles allows the mage to nudge things to their desired outcome more easily. A person who is already exhausted can be put to sleep with a Compelling rather than Weaving of Mind.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It may also provide inspiration for spells, such as comprehending neural networks might inspire a mage to use a Making to create an electronic intelligence using Forces, allowing it to &quot;Possess&quot; electronic devices. But ultimately you need to work within the set of possible symbols that define your Arcanum. Going beyond that might require a mundane solution, some kind of supernatural material, the aid of a supernatural being, adding conjunctional Arcana or just creative use of more spells to patch the flaws.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is no Consensus in Awakening. There is the Fallen with things that are, the Supernal with things that could be, the Abyss with things that cannot be and so on. But these are in no way informed by the thoughts of the masses, they are independent fundamental pillars of reality. Mages specialize in being able to search the nigh infinite possibility space of the Supernal and use it to overwrite reality.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-21-2022, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T10:50:38-08:00","id":1475458,"title":"","content":"So, if<br /> a) a wizard can make any (viable - what's viable?) lifeform with life without understanding it, perfectly.<br /> b) a wizard can make a projector (which will work), and that will have all the internal information on tags even.<br /> <br /> That means that the Information on the details of what's done is not needed to be known by the mage, and is brought from the Supernal along with the spell. So can a mage create a book that has 'the information I need at the moment - written by Hemingway', with just the Matter arcana and intent? At which point does it stop being viable to bring information along with the effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T12:24:16-08:00","id":1475462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475458#post1475458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if<br /> a) a wizard can make any (viable - what's viable?) lifeform with life without understanding it, perfectly.<br /> b) a wizard can make a projector (which will work), and that will have all the internal information on tags even.<br /> <br /> That means that the Information on the details of what's done is not needed to be known by the mage, and is brought from the Supernal along with the spell. So can a mage create a book that has 'the information I need at the moment - written by Hemingway', with just the Matter arcana and intent? At which point does it stop being viable to bring information along with the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe it would require more than Matter, but possible via conjunctional Arcana. You would need either a Ruling of Mind or Fate (to gain the equivalent of the Informed condition) to get the generic information on the topic. Written by Hemingway is more complicated, I think that would require some way to target a specific mind (since a mind is far more symbolically complex than a bar code), such as touching the person, using material yantra or perhaps create the equivalent with Infinite Monkey Theorem using Fate 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T13:52:07-08:00","id":1475467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475458#post1475458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means that the Information on the details of what's done is not needed to be known by the mage, and is brought from the Supernal along with the spell. So can a mage create a book that has 'the information I need at the moment - written by Hemingway', with just the Matter arcana and intent? At which point does it stop being viable to bring information along with the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a combined spell of \u201cLucky Number\u201d-Fate Ruling and a Matter/Time or Fate or Space Making. \u201cLucky number\u201d is for the information you don\u2019t have and are going to need, Matter is to make the material form of the book, and Time or Fate or Space can cause the thing to have been written by a particular person. The point of the spell is to acquire information you don\u2019t have, and that you would need, and that can just be done by \u201cLucky Number\u201d.<br /> <br /> Matter doesn\u2019t create anything not directly related to the object on it own, it doesn\u2019t have a history outside of just being there when the mage calls. You have to add that on with other Arcana. Matter also has nothing to do with information you don\u2019t have, unless that information is directly Matter related. Think more; what is this weapon made out of, and what\u2019s the boiling point of fluoride, and less; who used this weapon, and what boiled that fluoride? Technically I suppose you could force a book to appear with everything you don\u2019t know on it, but that would be a infinitely sized book since there is infinite information you don\u2019t know. Or has the text so fine it\u2019s impossible to read. So you need to know what you don\u2019t know to reduce the information volume. Even if you do know what you need to know, Fate is required to make a filter to make the spell usable, and at that point, why don\u2019t you just ask Fate directly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-25-2022, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T15:36:10-08:00","id":1475471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475458#post1475458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a) a wizard can make any (viable - what's viable?) lifeform with life without understanding it, perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life mages don't have to make &quot;viable&quot; Life forms, if you want a cat with function wings you can do that too. It's just harder.<br /> <br /> And what I think this premise misses is that the Life mages <b>understand</b> Life phenomena, but their understanding is rooted in Supernal wisdom instead of Fallen rules. They understand &quot;cat&quot; by seeing the Supernal symbolism that goes into &quot;cat.&quot; Mages don't need to study genetics to understand how wild-type cats domesticated into cats with various genetic markers that can be inherited into what we call cat breeds. All of the biology that explains how an Cornish Rex, a Maine Coon, and an English short hair are all the same species with some minor genetic quirks maintained by artificial selection isn't important to mages. Mages can see the Supernal ideal of &quot;cat&quot; along with the variants of &quot;cat&quot; in Supernal Life that specify &quot;male cat with a tuxedo coat.&quot;<br /> <br /> What they don't need to understand is the Fallen World's scientific rules of &quot;cat&quot; in order to perfectly make a cat with magic. They need to understand it, just from a different source of understanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That means that the Information on the details of what's done is not needed to be known by the mage, and is brought from the Supernal along with the spell. </div> </div> </div>This has been covered. The mage needs to bring in details not covered by the Supernal ideals they understand. The Supernal ideal of &quot;projectors&quot; includes having a serial number. But unless the mage bring the detailed knowledge of a specific serial number, they can't actualize that specific serial number into existence. If they can't pull a trick like, &quot;the serial number of the projector owned by this specific person,&quot; if they don't know what that serial number is already. Magic requires forming the imago, and the imago will be incomplete with that gap in the mage's knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So can a mage create a book that has 'the information I need at the moment - written by Hemingway', with just the Matter arcana and intent? </div> </div> </div>No, because they need to be able to form an imago of what's in the book. They can make a book, it might even have words and such in it, but without knowing what they want in the book, Matter can't make the up for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At which point does it stop being viable to bring information along with the effect? </div> </div> </div>When the information isn't a Fallen reflection of the Supernal ideal being translated. The &quot;information&quot; on cat genetics comes along because cat genetics is a Fallen translation of Supernal symbols. Matter can't summon Hemmingway to write down secrets you don't know, because that's not part of the Supernal symbol of &quot;book.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T16:34:32-08:00","id":1475472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475467#post1475467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a combined spell of \u201cLucky Number\u201d-Fate Ruling and a Matter/Time or Fate or Space Making. \u201cLucky number\u201d is for the information you don\u2019t have and are going to need, Matter is to make the material form of the book, and Time or Fate or Space can cause the thing to have been written by a particular person. The point of the spell is to acquire information you don\u2019t have, and that you would need, and that can just be done by \u201cLucky Number\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this is a case where I think there is actually relevance to understanding who spells in general and some of the specific examples function, so that one has a working idea of what to extrapolate from them for creative thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> So as a reminder: Lucky Number does not produce information, it significantly focuses the odds of a random selection of numbers or letters being useful. It works according to a logic of it being plausible, but highly unlikely, that a first guess at what a password will be correct, and kind of brute forces fate in the direction of that improbable circumstance. I think it can reasonably be assumed to be something that works because the parameters are fairly straightforward.<br /> <br /> A million monkeys working at a million typewriters might eventually produce the works of Shakespeare, but I don't think a Ruling of Fate can guide directly to that outcome, because it has too many moving parts. Even something like a Patterning such as Strings of Fate can designate an outcome, but needs to let the sequence of events that leads up to it work itself out according to a plausible timescale over which the mage has little fine control.<br /> <br /> That, I think, precludes mages can being able to use Fate at the conventional levels to make it so that when they make a stab at guessing something like complex or specific information as yet unknown to them, or fully replicate an individual's writing style or something, their first go at it happens to get everything right the first time. You <i>could</i> use Strings of Fate to put yourself on the path to discovering a desired secret, but it's going to need time to get done (and possibly some degree of the mage forfeiting a bit of agency in how they act while the spell works, at least insofar as they need to follow the paths offered for them).<br /> <br /> I think this outlook holds up logically, but more importantly, it means that the objectives in a game predicated on the idea that characters go out to uncover mysteries and discover information isn't totally overridden by a two dot spell that can allow them to know basically whatever they want from the outset conjured from nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T01:33:15-08:00","id":1475484,"title":"","content":"A Matter / Life mage can Make a book / cat. Not a specific book / cat.<br /> <br /> Sure you can create a cat with particular features, such as an eye injury, particular pattern of fur or extra gills. <br /> <br /> Likewise you can make a book with features, like hardback, pop-up pictures, or built-in flamethrower attachments.<br /> <br /> You can't make a specific cat which was at the scene of the crime you are investigating and so has a specific memory of what happened (with only Life). Similarly you can't make a specific book which happens to be filled with specific information with matter alone.<br /> <br /> Sidenite: you can make a digital book with forces (even though the hard drive you are storing it in is in the domain of matter, flipping the bits is something you can do with forces...) But you still don't get specific information like that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: it seems fate would be entirely capable of producing circumstances where the book simply arrived in your hands, maybe a delivery driver makes a mistake and leaves it at your door when someone else ordered it.<br /> <br /> The difficulty depends on how improbable the circumstances required are.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: the only contrary point of view is that i have seen Dave B discuss Death being used to create the Ghost of a specific person. If anyone can find that conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-26-2022, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T02:53:08-08:00","id":1475485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475484#post1475484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Matter / Life mage can Make a book / cat. Not a specific book / cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important nitpick:<br /> <br /> A mage can make a specific book/cat with just that Arcana <b>if they already know enough about it.</b> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T05:49:02-08:00","id":1475486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475484#post1475484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT2: the only contrary point of view is that i have seen Dave B discuss Death being used to create the Ghost of a specific person. If anyone can find that conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a forum conversation, that's the text of the Create Ghost spell:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage creates a ghost within Twilight. She can fashion the ghost as an echo of another person, either alive or dead, though the ghost is not the actual person. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T11:12:51-08:00","id":1475498,"title":"","content":"I get the impression that familiarity with Geist Second Edition would give a lot of perspective on what can be made of ghosts. Literal phantom limbs and all.<br /> <br /> On reflection, my prior assessment of using Fate to benefit coming to a viable conclusion based on guesswork has been revised a bit. It wouldn't function along the lines of Lucky Number, but using a Blessing to acquire the Informed or Inspired Condition, maybe combined with something to offset penalties, would plausibly extend the extent of what somebody could hit upon by chance through a straightforward Skill roll. Probably still generally lacks the specificity of exactly replicating the style of an author that you haven't read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T04:49:21-08:00","id":1475529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475485#post1475485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Important nitpick:<br /> <br /> A mage can make a specific book/cat with just that Arcana <b>if they already know enough about it.</b> </div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that is an interesting point. I still think, creating a specific cat - with the memories of what it saw last night - requires more. Like, creating that cat is fine, but it doesn't necessarily remember everything i has for lunch... <br /> <br /> Whereas creating a specific book would require the specific information, like you'd have to know what the information was supposed to be...<br /> <br /> @Satchel<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not a forum conversation, that's the text of the Create Ghost spell: </div> </div> </div>You're right, the forum conversation i was misremembering was about the limits of that spell, if any.<br /> <br /> But similar to my comments on creating a cat. If you create the Ghost of a Seer Minister, and then try to interrogate it for information. What limits would there be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T05:34:35-08:00","id":1475530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475529#post1475529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But similar to my comments on creating a cat. If you create the Ghost of a Seer Minister, and then try to interrogate it for information. What limits would there be?</div> </div> </div> </div>On that front, in relation to a question about if the created ghost of a person had their memories:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1134401#post1134401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They get as much memory of the original person as a regular ghost does (that is, full of holes and prone to one-track-mindism).</div> </div> </div> </div>Relatedly, while it's not as directly relevant in a game where they're not PCs or directly adjacent phenomena to PCs, Geist's rules for the Absent and the related facts of Memory trading paint a particular picture of the above, and its more detailed writeup on ghosts in general emphasizes that even self-aware ghosts have sometimes-significant gaps in their memories.<br /> <br /> And that is, of course, to say nothing of the issue of actually <i>knowing</i> who a particular Seer Minister is, given that such a person is a leader in a wildly competitive Sect that makes regular use of bodyjacking Artifacts for a wide variety of reasons, including rampant eminently-sensible paranoia of this exact sort of thing happening to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-27-2022, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T08:55:36-08:00","id":1475536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475530#post1475530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that front, in relation to a question about if the created ghost of a person had their memories:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Relatedly, while it's not as directly relevant in a game where they're not PCs or directly adjacent phenomena to PCs, Geist's rules for the Absent and the related facts of Memory trading paint a particular picture of the above, and its more detailed writeup on ghosts in general emphasizes that even self-aware ghosts have sometimes-significant gaps in their memories.<br /> <br /> And that is, of course, to say nothing of the issue of actually <i>knowing</i> who a particular Seer Minister is, given that such a person is a leader in a wildly competitive Sect that makes regular use of bodyjacking Artifacts for a wide variety of reasons, including rampant eminently-sensible paranoia of this exact sort of thing happening to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, and yes, i think the requirement of knowing who the target is there is the same as discussed for knowing the cat as discussed previously (it is just harder to know...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475537#post1475537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">continued here.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-27-2022, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T11:43:22-08:00","id":1475545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475530#post1475530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is, of course, to say nothing of the issue of actually <i>knowing</i> who a particular Seer Minister is, given that such a person is a leader in a wildly competitive Sect that makes regular use of bodyjacking Artifacts for a wide variety of reasons, including rampant eminently-sensible paranoia of this exact sort of thing happening to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My read on the description in the core is that in Second Edition, even Lesser Ministers are liable to be living pretty much full time in Exarchate Verges with a few Ochemata attending to them (at least so long as their Ministry has some decent substance), never mind how the Greater Ministers are archmasters with their brains directly jacked into their patrons and residing in hereditary Chantries. I think that for the Pentacle any Minister worthy of the title is mostly going to come across as a rumour and a distant name.<br /> <br /> Plus how Signs of Sorcery has that whole line about how the operational playbook says to regard any tetrarch or Minister as an archmaster unless proven otherwise. It might be that a Minister is active enough for somebody to get a profile of them that could be used to make their ghost, but such a thing could be a really bad idea if you don't know what kinds of crazy things they might turn out to be able to exercise through such ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T12:29:28-08:00","id":1475549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475545#post1475545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My read on the description in the core is that in Second Edition, even Lesser Ministers are liable to be living pretty much full time in Exarchate Verges with a few Ochemata attending to them (at least so long as their Ministry has some decent substance), never mind how the Greater Ministers are archmasters with their brains directly jacked into their patrons and residing in hereditary Chantries. I think that for the Pentacle any Minister worthy of the title is mostly going to come across as a rumour and a distant name.<br /> <br /> Plus how Signs of Sorcery has that whole line about how the operational playbook says to regard any tetrarch or Minister as an archmaster unless proven otherwise. It might be that a Minister is active enough for somebody to get a profile of them that could be used to make their ghost, but such a thing could be a really bad idea if you don't know what kinds of crazy things they might turn out to be able to exercise through such ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that level of power and distance, i think it is more likely one would start with a low ranking Seer who can be identified... Then find out more intel from their ghost. Possibly use info to incriminate the seer in question or attempt to move up the ranks - though using the same tactic more than once may risk serious backlash.<br /> <br /> On the converse, what sort of powers might they be able to exercise through such ghosts? How would they even know it existed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T12:56:23-08:00","id":1475552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475471#post1475471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life mages don't have to make &quot;viable&quot; Life forms, if you want a cat with function wings you can do that too. It's just harder.<br /> <br /> And what I think this premise misses is that the Life mages <b>understand</b> Life phenomena, but their understanding is rooted in Supernal wisdom instead of Fallen rules. They understand &quot;cat&quot; by seeing the Supernal symbolism that goes into &quot;cat.&quot; Mages don't need to study genetics to understand how wild-type cats domesticated into cats with various genetic markers that can be inherited into what we call cat breeds. All of the biology that explains how an Cornish Rex, a Maine Coon, and an English short hair are all the same species with some minor genetic quirks maintained by artificial selection isn't important to mages. Mages can see the Supernal ideal of &quot;cat&quot; along with the variants of &quot;cat&quot; in Supernal Life that specify &quot;male cat with a tuxedo coat.&quot;<br /> <br /> What they don't need to understand is the Fallen World's scientific rules of &quot;cat&quot; in order to perfectly make a cat with magic. They need to understand it, just from a different source of understanding.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But you can copy a specific cat, right? Where do you get the information for the specific cat? Also, if one cat has a chip, and the mage used matter, would the information for the chip come from the imago as well?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> This has been covered. The mage needs to bring in details not covered by the Supernal ideals they understand. The Supernal ideal of &quot;projectors&quot; includes having a serial number. But unless the mage bring the detailed knowledge of a specific serial number, they can't actualize that specific serial number into existence. If they can't pull a trick like, &quot;the serial number of the projector owned by this specific person,&quot; if they don't know what that serial number is already. Magic requires forming the imago, and the imago will be incomplete with that gap in the mage's knowledge.<br /> </div> </div> </div>So, it seems that a mage couldn't create from thin air 'mike's car keys', since this involves information (the key's secret), that the mage does not have, right? <br /> <br /> But could they bring in firmware that would be needed in some electronic, or the manual for the projector? Could they restore a book from the final piece of it, if there were no other copies, and the mage never read it?<br /> <br /> Could I make a exact replica of someone's laptop with matter, with the same data inside of it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, because they need to be able to form an imago of what's in the book. They can make a book, it might even have words and such in it, but without knowing what they want in the book, Matter can't make the up for them. </div> </div> </div>He knows what he wants: a book that gives him the information he needs at this moment. It's vague, sure, but that's what he wants. Or maybe, more specifically, he needs a book that gives information on the weakness of a specific type of spirit in the Shadow. Does the mage need to know the information in the book to make it? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the information isn't a Fallen reflection of the Supernal ideal being translated. The &quot;information&quot; on cat genetics comes along because cat genetics is a Fallen translation of Supernal symbols. Matter can't summon Hemmingway to write down secrets you don't know, because that's not part of the Supernal symbol of &quot;book.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It's in the Supernal symbol of 'Hypothethic Books by Hemingway', that could be as much of a symbol as 'ideal domestic cat that is common for this region' (there should be plenty of hypothetical books in temenos, right!?). How specific can you get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T13:02:26-08:00","id":1475553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475552#post1475552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can copy a specific cat, right? Where do you get the information for the specific cat?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the cat that you're copying. Which you presumably know about in more than hypothetical terms, because you're trying to copy it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if one cat has a chip, and the mage used matter, would the information for the chip come from the imago as well? </div> </div> </div>You would need Forces to put the relevant data on the chip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, it seems that a mage couldn't create from thin air 'mike's car keys', since this involves information (the key's secret), that the mage does not have, right? </div> </div> </div>If you don't have the keys or the lock they go to, you don't have the referent needed to produce a key that fits that lock.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But could they bring in firmware that would be needed in some electronic, or the manual for the projector? Could they restore a book from the final piece of it, if there were no other copies, and the mage never read it? </div> </div> </div>If you have the last piece of the book, you have a piece of the book to rebuild it from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could I make a exact replica of someone's laptop with matter, with the same data inside of it? </div> </div> </div>As above, the data inside of it would be a Forces pattern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He knows what he wants: a book that gives him the information he needs at this moment. It's vague, sure, but that's what he wants. Or maybe, more specifically, he needs a book that gives information on the weakness of a specific type of spirit in the Shadow. Does the mage need to know the information in the book to make it? </div> </div> </div>If he is not pulling from a book that already exists, he is making the book himself, and if he is making the book himself, he needs to know its contents for them to be useful. If he wants that information, he needs to use an Arcanum capable of getting it, in this case being Spirit (possibly Space, if the spirit in question is not present for the casting).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's in the Supernal symbol of 'Hypothethic Books by Hemingway', that could be as much of a symbol as 'ideal domestic cat that is common for this region' (there should be plenty of hypothetical books in temenos, right!?). How specific can you get? </div> </div> </div>Hypothetical books in the Temenos would contain the unconscious expectations of whatever subset of humanity imagines them, based on the narratives and themes of that part of the Temenos. The Temenos is not the infinite continuum of possible information, much less information with a specific presentation \u2014 things exist there when they've been shared with people, not as pre-realized ideas you can pluck from the ether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475549#post1475549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the converse, what sort of powers might they be able to exercise through such ghosts? How would they even know it existed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries alludes to its sample Tetrarch having been granted an Artifact described in Seers of the Throne, the Mask of Eyes, that lets its user pick what they want to see and view it through any nearby representation of a human eye. It does not use the known laws of sympathy to accomplish this. The Artifact is a mark of favor from the Eye and is speculated to be either a Supernal creation or the product of archmastery.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of shit archmasters can get up to, and Ministers are assumed by the Pentacle to be archmasters until proven otherwise. It would not do to assume it's <i>not</i> within the power of a Minister to exploit a ghost made in their own image, because the price of being wrong in that assumption could be your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-27-2022, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T17:25:34-08:00","id":1475563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475552#post1475552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the Supernal symbol of 'Hypothethic Books by Hemingway', that could be as much of a symbol as 'ideal domestic cat that is common for this region'</div> </div> </div> </div>It really shouldn't. Look at some of the Platonic ideas that are an inspiration for what the Supernal is about; you're not quite limited to the extent of truly mathematically perfect triangles, but it's similar.<br /> <br /> Supernal symbols don't take the form of every specific instance, they'd be more in the ballpark of the concept of a writer's creativity, of which anything to do with Hemmingway, real or potential, is but an imperfect instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(there should be plenty of hypothetical books in temenos, right!?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, although they'd be limited by the understanding and imagination of human speculation. You summon something like that out of the Astral Realms and you get something cobbled together from Hemmingway's impressions and everybody who's ever tried to imagine further or alternative books that he might have written. The worst kind of art by committee; it certainly won't be an objective assessment of what he could have done, and probably won't be that compelling to read in its own right, either garbled incomprehensibly or very generic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T15:02:51-08:00","id":1475597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Temenos is not the infinite continuum of possible information, much less information with a specific presentation \u2014 things exist there when they've been shared with people, not as pre-realized ideas you can pluck from the ether </div> </div> </div>Yes, you want pre-realized ideas plucked from the ether, you gotta go to the Abyss... (Aka come to the dark side we have pizza).<br /> <br /> At least by one interpretation, everything that doesn't exist is the Abyss. Unfortunately that includes an infinite number of things which you don't really want, and perhaps they hate reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-28-2022, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T14:27:11-08:00","id":1475941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475553#post1475553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the cat that you're copying. Which you presumably know about in more than hypothetical terms, because you're trying to copy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so I need to scan and understand a cat to copy it? Do I have to feed this information to the supernal, or does it already have it? Or do I just need to point to the Supernal - 'I want something exactly like this'? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You would need Forces to put the relevant data on the chip. </div> </div> </div>Why? would I need Forces to make anything with firmware? Is forces+matter needed to create a magnet, even if magnetism is an arrangement of matter? If I copy a computer, would it come without an OS?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't have the keys or the lock they go to, you don't have the referent needed to produce a key that fits that lock. </div> </div> </div>So if I can create a key based on a lock, I can create information (key) based on a problem (lock), right? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have the last piece of the book, you have a piece of the book to rebuild it from. </div> </div> </div>But the information that was on the other pages is not there in the piece. It's just a piece of paper with a very limited part of the information the book had. Where does the rest of the information come from? The information in the book was destroyed with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As above, the data inside of it would be a Forces pattern. </div> </div> </div>So even the information on a magnetic drive that is turned off is Forces?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If he is not pulling from a book that already exists, he is making the book himself, and if he is making the book himself, he needs to know its contents for them to be useful. If he wants that information, he needs to use an Arcanum capable of getting it, in this case being Spirit (possibly Space, if the spirit in question is not present for the casting). </div> </div> </div>In the beginning of this discussion, we mentioned that you could make a 'perfect' projector without knowledge from projectors whatsoever, and that a mage didn't need more than matter, just the concept of the object was enough. I want a book with some information, if there was a similar anywhere else in the world, could I ask for a generic version? Could I use the fact that I could not conjure the book to identify that a book like this does not exist in the current world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hypothetical books in the Temenos would contain the unconscious expectations of whatever subset of humanity imagines them, based on the narratives and themes of that part of the Temenos. The Temenos is not the infinite continuum of possible information, much less information with a specific presentation \u2014 things exist there when they've been shared with people, not as pre-realized ideas you can pluck from the ether. </div> </div> </div>From what I've read recently (Astral Realms), the unwritten books of dead authors are there in the Temenos. So how come only things that existed or were discussed are there?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T15:09:00-08:00","id":1475943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475941#post1475941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so I need to scan and understand a cat to copy it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages have mage sight. They can see the Supernal symbols that underlay the Fallen phenomena in front of them. By &quot;scan&quot; this jut means, &quot;perceive the cat as a mage, not a normal human.&quot; No in depth applications of mage sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do I have to feed this information to the supernal, or does it already have it? Or do I just need to point to the Supernal - 'I want something exactly like this'? </div> </div> </div>You, being a mage that has an understanding of the supernal nature behind the specific cat in front of you form an imago in your head of a duplication of that cluster of symbols, and then bring those supernal truths into existence.<br /> <br /> And can you please actually try to apply the logic of the game here? Your questions feel less like &quot;I'm struggling to understand this,&quot; and more, &quot;I want to show this is all non-sense so I don't have to understand it by asking the right question to destroy everyone else's explanations.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? </div> </div> </div>Forces governs energy fields that aren't the natural properties of other patterns. Data doesn't just appear on storage devices. It's not property of the Supernal ideal of &quot;hard drive&quot; to have any specific data on it, so you have to put that data on it somehow.<br /> <br /> Though I would argue in the specific case of copying an existing cat that's got an ID chip on it, matter should be enough because you're duplicating a specific chip that's already in a specific configuration of matter to store that information, just like copying a book would copy the text inside of it. But like the projector discussion, if you weren't copying a specific existing chip, you would need Forces to program the chip yourself with data if you wanted to do that with magic.<br /> <br /> [quote]Is forces+matter needed to create a magnet, even if magnetism is an arrangement of matter?/quote]<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I copy a computer, would it come without an OS? </div> </div> </div>Again, if you're copying a specific extant computer, no. If you're creating a computer out of nothing, and want specific programs or data on it, you need Forces to manipulate that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if I can create a key based on a lock, I can create information (key) based on a problem (lock), right? </div> </div> </div>Not as generically as you seem to be implying.<br /> <br /> The key/lock thing works because there's a 1:1 physically correlation. Even if you don't actually end up with the precise key/lock that the owner of the complimentary item has, the fundamental shape of the key and the lock are intertwined. A normal person with the right knowledge and tools could look at a key, and build a lock that goes to it, and similarly look at a lock and build a key that matches it. Magic just skips past all that.<br /> <br /> If that 1:1 correlation isn't valid, then you can't magic the &quot;information&quot; from the problem. Basically, you can use magic to solve 1+3=X, but not X+Y=4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the information that was on the other pages is not there in the piece. </div> </div> </div>Having part of a pattern would let you find the Supernal full pattern and bring it into being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The information in the book was destroyed with it. </div> </div> </div>Only in the Fallen world (and then only maybe, it is possible for items to persist in other states of being within the Fallen world, like the Astral Realms). Trying to hide things from mages by just destroying their physical forms is a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want a book with some information, if there was a similar anywhere else in the world, could I ask for a generic version? Could I use the fact that I could not conjure the book to identify that a book like this does not exist in the current world? </div> </div> </div>Again, what about the whole imago forming process is not getting through here? A mage needs to be able to form the imago of the end result of the magic in their heads. They can't form an imago of something they don't know about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T16:24:11-08:00","id":1475951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475941#post1475941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so I need to scan and understand a cat to copy it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to know what cat you're copying to copy that cat. This is not a matter of spellcasting so much as the basic semantics of &quot;copying.&quot; If I tell you to draw the exact likeness of an image you haven't seen, you cannot do so until you've seen it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? </div> </div> </div>Because Forces is the Arcanum for patterns of energetic phenomena. It's the Gross counterpart of the Arcanum corresponding to things' essences and ideal forms \u2014 shapes and structures made of material phenomena less solid than flesh and stone, whether they're scheduling apps or storm systems, are handled by Forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if I can create a key based on a lock, I can create information (key) based on a problem (lock), right? </div> </div> </div>If you have a lock, you have a referent for &quot;key that fits this lock.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, this is not a spellcasting issue so much as a knowing-what-you're-trying-to-make thing. You wouldn't be able to specifically create a replacement part for a mechanical device without knowing what part was missing, but you could repair a broken device without knowing what parts were broken by virtue of knowing what the functioning device looks like in your mind's eye.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the information that was on the other pages is not there in the piece. It's just a piece of paper with a very limited part of the information the book had. Where does the rest of the information come from? The information in the book was destroyed with it. </div> </div> </div>A piece of the book still exists as a referent for the whole book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So even the information on a magnetic drive that is turned off is Forces? </div> </div> </div>Again: The issue you are running into here is a matter of <i>copying a specific laptop</i>. You can make an out-of-the-box laptop with Matter just fine, but if you want to impart specific data to it, particularly specific data that you don't have yourself, you're going to need the Arcanum that lets you read and write electronic information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the beginning of this discussion, we mentioned that you could make a 'perfect' projector without knowledge from projectors whatsoever, and that a mage didn't need more than matter, just the concept of the object was enough. </div> </div> </div>Right. Because you <i>know what a projector is</i>. If I ask you to make slood, you're not going to be able to do that unless you know what slood is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want a book with some information, if there was a similar anywhere else in the world, could I ask for a generic version? Could I use the fact that I could not conjure the book to identify that a book like this does not exist in the current world? </div> </div> </div>If you want a book with information and you don't know the information, your options are to seek out that information yourself and/or pull on Fate to nudge the world such that you come into possession of that information with a bit of legwork.<br /> <br /> Much like you can't use a Yantra for a symbolic correspondence you don't recognize, you can't create a spell whose end result at the point of casting is outside your ability to conceive of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I've read recently (Astral Realms), the unwritten books of dead authors are there in the Temenos. </div> </div> </div>Having reread the Temenos section of that book quite recently, I can only ask if you read it at all, because that's the exact opposite of how things are added to the Temenos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T02:32:12-08:00","id":1476034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475951#post1475951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having reread the Temenos section of that book quite recently, I can only ask if you read it at all, because that's the exact opposite of how things are added to the Temenos</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that only ideas shared between two humans exist in the Temenos, the more humans that have shared the idea then the easier it is to find in the Temenos... A dead author could have had in depth conversations with their publisher, but the wild fabric theories of millions of internet fans will be much more prominent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T13:34:01-08:00","id":1476113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475951#post1475951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to know what cat you're copying to copy that cat. This is not a matter of spellcasting so much as the basic semantics of &quot;copying.&quot; If I tell you to draw the exact likeness of an image you haven't seen, you cannot do so until you've seen it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But after I've seen it, I can copy it just fine, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because Forces is the Arcanum for patterns of energetic phenomena. It's the Gross counterpart of the Arcanum corresponding to things' essences and ideal forms \u2014 shapes and structures made of material phenomena less solid than flesh and stone, whether they're scheduling apps or storm systems, are handled by Forces. </div> </div> </div>Material magnetism has a pattern of energy as a consequence of an arrangement of matter. Anyway, so to do any engine (which has permanent magnets), you'd need forces as well. As well as loudspeakers, etc. Right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have a lock, you have a referent for &quot;key that fits this lock.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Even if the key no longer exists, the information comes from nothing, in this case. Right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, this is not a spellcasting issue so much as a knowing-what-you're-trying-to-make thing. You wouldn't be able to specifically create a replacement part for a mechanical device without knowing what part was missing, but you could repair a broken device without knowing what parts were broken by virtue of knowing what the functioning device looks like in your mind's eye. </div> </div> </div>So you need previous knowledge to do it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A piece of the book still exists as a referent for the whole book. </div> </div> </div>But you do not need to know the contents of the book this way, right? There is no more information on this piece of paper than any other. The information has to come from somewhere. Unless it's a special kind of sympathy?<br /> <br /> And, say, a book on the weakness of a spirit is referent to the spirit, right? So if I meet the spirit, I can create a book based on its weakness, because it's all connected, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again: The issue you are running into here is a matter of <i>copying a specific laptop</i>. You can make an out-of-the-box laptop with Matter just fine, but if you want to impart specific data to it, particularly specific data that you don't have yourself, you're going to need the Arcanum that lets you read and write electronic information. </div> </div> </div>So I can generate a laptop with an OS without forces if I am not copying a laptop? I thought you just declared that Forces was necessary to make any patterns on a disk drive?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right. Because you <i>know what a projector is</i>. If I ask you to make slood, you're not going to be able to do that unless you know what slood is. </div> </div> </div>But I don't need to know any details, magic handwaves it for me! I know what a book is. Why can't magic handwave the details?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want a book with information and you don't know the information, your options are to seek out that information yourself and/or pull on Fate to nudge the world such that you come into possession of that information with a bit of legwork. </div> </div> </div>You are creating information from nowhere when you create a projector. One could learn to work on projectors by opening one it created up. One could create the maintenance manual from one projector (key) from the projector (door). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much like you can't use a Yantra for a symbolic correspondence you don't recognize, you can't create a spell whose end result at the point of casting is outside your ability to conceive of. </div> </div> </div>But you can do create the whole inside of something you've never seen, and have it working. Magic even has the creativity of making a generic, fully functional version of a projector with every component inside being placed in a way that makes sense to humans. Why can't I have the insides of a book?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having reread the Temenos section of that book quite recently, I can only ask if you read it at all, because that's the exact opposite of how things are added to the Temenos. </div> </div> </div>This was my bad - I have rechecked now and couldn't find any quotes to sustain what I said about unwritten books. I have been reading mage for another game, along with several other things, so I was bound to misremember something. I think that the cause for my error was because I read in the MtA Core 2nd about the Temenos: 'You can meet (...) every fiction. ', and I jumped to the conclusion that it was every fiction written or not. Wrong, anyway.<br /> <br /> But since we talked about a book on spirits written by Hemingway, the concept is there now. All that's missing are the details, but True Magick deals with the details, right? :-P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T13:56:25-08:00","id":1476114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476113#post1476113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But after I've seen it, I can copy it just fine, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally. Though the ST could ask you to make a memory roll for anything complicated enough that fine details are going to matter if they wanted to. The default rules don't require that though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if the key no longer exists, the information comes from nothing, in this case. Right? </div> </div> </div>No, the information comes from the lock. The lock knows what shape key unlocks it, because that's a fundamental part of the lock's pattern. That's the whole point. It doesn't come from &quot;nothing&quot; it comes from a referent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you need previous knowledge to do it? </div> </div> </div>Yet again: put this in the context of how forming an imago works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The information has to come from somewhere. Unless it's a special kind of sympathy? </div> </div> </div>The information comes for the undamaged Supernal ideal of the book, which exists even if the physical version is damaged. You could, in a metaphysical and not rules sense, see this as a form of sympathy,but it's not special. This is the connection between all individual Fallen phenomena and the Supernal reality behind them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if I meet the spirit, I can create a book based on its weakness, because it's all connected, right? </div> </div> </div>Did you determine what the spirit's weakness is to have that information to form an imago of a book that discusses it? A spirit, unlike a cat, is a supernatural entity with some protections over its true nature being perceived. Mages aren't going to be stymied for long on this, but it would require more than a casual glance at the spirit to accomplish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't need to know any details, magic handwaves it for me! I know what a book is. Why can't magic handwave the details? </div> </div> </div>Because you're playing a mage that's doing magic, and the mage has to form an imago of the effect for it to take place.<br /> <br /> I'm really not sure why you're ignoring this fundamental part of spell casting in the system: the mage needs to be able of visualize the final result of the spells in their mind. Magic &quot;handwaves&quot; transforming Supernal truths into Fallen phenomena, but it can only do that guided by the imago the mage creates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are creating information from nowhere when you create a projector. </div> </div> </div>No, you're using your knowledge of projectors being a thing to form an imago of a projector in your head, and then using the information stored in the Supernal truth that defines projectors to fill in the reality of the projector as it comes into being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why can't I have the insides of a book? </div> </div> </div>You can have all the insides of the book you want. It just isn't going to be arranged in the specific fashion you want. A book full of pages and pages of lorem ipsum has all of the insides of a book, arranged how a human understands them, in a function that acts as a book. It's just relatively worthless because the text conveys no useful information. If you want it to have useful information, that information has to come from somewhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T14:28:12-08:00","id":1476118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476113#post1476113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Magick deals with the details, right? :-P</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of Mage: the Ascension in how you're approaching this whole issue (right down, honestly, to how there are a lot of Ascension arguments about the hypothetical proceedings of magic that are divorced from what goes on at an actual table; have you had a player say they're trying to conjure Hemingway's lost novel?). It's a nitpick in terminology here, but just as a reminder, there ain't no True Magick here. You don't wish for a thing through enlightened willpower alone. There's supernal sorcery. It works, as Heavy Arms says, through clearly glimpsing the desired supernal symbols using your gnosis, and imposing them on the world:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage imagines each part of the spell in her mind before she casts it, envisioning the Imago of the spell. The Imago is the mental representation of the end result of the spell including all its effects and factors. Without the Imago, the mage is incapable of fully envisioning what she wants to impart into the world, her will incapable of imprinting the truth without a defined Pattern. </div> </div> </div>You can envision the Platonic ideal of a projector and impose that ideal onto the Phenomenal World. There is a shared &quot;projectorness&quot; that all projectors share in; you are glimpsing that form in the Supernal Realm and calling it into being to incarnate in the world of material shape and mechanism. Provided, of course, you have enough Gnosis, the insight to see beyond the real into the true, and respective Arcanum, the secret understanding of the relevant symbols and the way they interact with phenomenal reality. There are different shapes a projector can take, by different manufacture, but they don't deviate from that shared &quot;projectorness&quot; you are calling on.<br /> <br /> You can't envision the Platonic ideal of Hemingway's lost novel because there is no one Platonic ideal of Hemingway's lost novel: there are infinite possible variations of the novel Hemingway never wrote, and you don't know which one you're trying to call. If you knew the words to the novel then you could make a book with those words in it. The Arcanum of Matter contains all possible configurations of ink on paper, but not the mechanisms to determine which ones Hemingway would have written. You'd honestly have better luck trying to conjure a simulacrum of Hemingway and making him write a novel. That will still be a novel by the simulacrum of Hemingway you made, but it's a lot more feasible for a Traveler on the Path.<br /> <br /> (An archmaster, an imperial magus beyond the limits of the five dot ratings in the corebook who has successfully undergone a Threshold Seeking to evolve and reshape his gnosis, could probably much more closely approximate the spell you keep trying to argue. It would almost certainly require the sixth-dot Practice of Dynamics, the ability for a spell that self-evolves, takes in outside information and grows accordingly. As an Imperial Practice, just casting this spell would not only require archmastery, but the location and sacrifice of a rare type of yantra unique to the spell, such as in this case, say, maybe unspent ink that had touched Hemingway's living hand.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-09-2022, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T17:31:59-08:00","id":1476129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476113#post1476113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But after I've seen it, I can copy it just fine, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. You can make a calico cat that looks like a calico cat that you have seen by having seen that calico cat, to the extent that you have seen that cat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Material magnetism has a pattern of energy as a consequence of an arrangement of matter. Anyway, so to do any engine (which has permanent magnets), you'd need forces as well. As well as loudspeakers, etc. Right? </div> </div> </div>You presumably know what a magnet is, what an engine is, what a loudspeaker is, et cetera, and can conceive of a magnet/engine/loudspeaker based on that knowledge without needing to specifically tweak the contents of that magnet/engine/loudspeaker in a fashion that would fall under the purview of Forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if the key no longer exists, the information comes from nothing, in this case. Right? </div> </div> </div>Wrong. There is a mechanical device designed to hold things together until certain of its components are moved to a specific configuration, and the shape of an object necessary to move those components into that configuration is information that exists already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you need previous knowledge to do it? </div> </div> </div>You need to <i>know what you are attempting to accomplish</i>. If you've never seen the color blue you're not going to be able to conceive of a blue rock and therefore won't be able to turn a rock blue. If you've never seen an ostrich you're not going to be able to give a pig the head of an ostrich. If you've never heard Beethoven's 5th you're not going to be able to make a spell that turns traffic noise into Beethoven's 5th.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you do not need to know the contents of the book this way, right? There is no more information on this piece of paper than any other. The information has to come from somewhere. Unless it's a special kind of sympathy? </div> </div> </div>The information comes from the book that existed and is part of the history of the piece of the book that you are using to reconstruct it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, say, a book on the weakness of a spirit is referent to the spirit, right? So if I meet the spirit, I can create a book based on its weakness, because it's all connected, right? </div> </div> </div>If you meet the spirit and you have the Spirit Arcanum, which is the Arcanum for finding out the weaknesses of spirits, you can find out the weakness of that spirit and can create a book containing that knowledge. The contents of a book are almost categorically specific information that you would need to build into the Imago to produce, because containing the weakness of a given spirit is not an intrinsic property of Books alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I can generate a laptop with an OS without forces if I am not copying a laptop? I thought you just declared that Forces was necessary to make any patterns on a disk drive? </div> </div> </div>You know what a laptop looks like. If you are not trying to write a specific pattern of information onto that laptop, you do not need the ability to rewrite the electronic contents of that laptop to contain the things that make a laptop work like A Laptop. I can make a fresh MacBook without needing to know machine code, but I'm not going to be able to make a MacBook with a PDF library full of all the Medieval Lit books my college courses didn't cover without knowing the contents of those books and the magical means of translating them into bits and bytes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't need to know any details, magic handwaves it for me! I know what a book is. Why can't magic handwave the details? </div> </div> </div>Because in this case the details are the specific point of the spell you are trying to cast. You can make a book with whatever contents you can imagine, but creating specific contents requires you to know what specific contents you want to make, and books are one type of object for which lacking that knowledge makes the ability to create A Book kind of useless for the purposes of brushing up on your studies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are creating information from nowhere when you create a projector. </div> </div> </div>Maybe in a theoretical physics sense, sure, but the metaphysics of Awakened magic are such that the existence of projectors means you're not creating information when you use magic to create a projector save in the sense that a projector now materially exists in a particular time and place for the duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But since we talked about a book on spirits written by Hemingway, the concept is there now. All that's missing are the details, but True Magick deals with the details, right? :-P </div> </div> </div>I am not a Hemingway scholar and presumably neither are you, and presumably neither are most of the people reading this conversation, to say nothing of our relative knowledge of spirits.<br /> <br /> The concept of a book on spirits written by Hemingway that exists in the Temenos would contain the collective unconscious idea of a book on spirits written by Hemingway as archetypally imagined by the bunch of us together; it might potentially be a very solid facsimile of what such a book would look like, but the contents wouldn't necessarily be accurate to how the denizens of the Shadow work or what Hemingway would've actually thought about them (not being a Hemingway scholar, I cannot say for certain how much of an occultist Ernest Hemingway was, but I don't imagine a book on spirits written by the genuine article would be too accurate, either).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T19:00:29-08:00","id":1476136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476129#post1476129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(not being a Hemingway scholar, I cannot say for certain how much of an occultist Ernest Hemingway was, but I don't imagine a book on spirits written by the genuine article would be too accurate, either).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given he doesn't come up* in occult discourse amongst sociologists, scholars, and practitioners, not much of one.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> As the larger discourse is going, I'm in the camp of wondering to what purpose all the scrutiny is going towards, particularly since A) none of this seems to be of particular assistance to the original poster's query, and B) it seems more like there's a goal of just maintaining a state of disbelief about the methodology of Awakening magic until someone throws their hands up in the air and says &quot;Fine, whatever&quot;-which, honestly, will happen with any magic system you test against, because <i>fiction.</i><br /> <br /> So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1524_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1524\" data-vbnamecard=\"1524\">pcontop</a> , kindly refresh me on what you're trying to do with this ongoing frain of questioning, because I would <i>love</i> to be dissuaded of the notion that point B is the current point of the conversation.<br /> <br /> *much, because Hemingway is <i>that</i> kind of asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T19:39:32-08:00","id":1476138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1524_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1524\" data-vbnamecard=\"1524\">pcontop</a> , kindly refresh me on what you're trying to do with this ongoing frain of questioning, because I would <i>love</i> to be dissuaded of the notion that point B is the current point of the conversation. </div> </div> </div> Assuming for a moment that the thread is a sincere attempt to understand Awakening\u2019s metaphysics, could you perhaps explain what you are having difficulty accepting or understanding ? Because we seem to be at at point in the normal conversation where everyone is repeating themselves endlessly, which isn\u2019t a good state to be in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476136#post1476136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*much, because Hemingway is <i>that</i> kind of asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div> What does this mean? I haven\u2019t read or heard anything substantial about him, so I\u2019m really curious.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T19:52:32-08:00","id":1476139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476113#post1476113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you do not need to know the contents of the book this way, right? There is no more information on this piece of paper than any other. The information has to come from somewhere. Unless it's a special kind of sympathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep ignoring the very premises of the game, especially the role of the Supernal in it, but also the Imago.<br /> <br /> First: no magic creates information out of nothing, ever. It doesn't matter with Arcanum you use or how, the information is always coming from somewhere, first and foremost from the Supernal, although not always.<br /> <br /> Second: magic is not handwaving information for you. Quite the opposite, information is <b>the thing</b> magic can't handwave for you. <i>Working on a distinct set of natural rules isn't the same as not knowing the rules</i>.<br /> <br /> This is why the Mage can create a projector with Matter. The Mage <b>knows</b> how the projector works <i>from a supernal perspective</i>. The Mage analysed projectors before with Mage Sight, or somehow learned how the <i>idea of a projector</i> is in details, so they can <i>picture the Supernal form of a projector exactly</i>.<br /> <br /> It is just as complete and elaborate as knowing the complete blueprint of a projector, actually even better. Then the Mage forms an Imago with <i>every single detail needed</i> for this idea, and brings the Supernal projector to the Fallen World. The fact the Mage doesn't know how the projector looks like inside in the Fallen World matters as much as an Astrophysicist not knowing how Neptune feels to the touch. It isn't the actual information that makes the actual thing be a thing.<br /> <br /> At no point information was created from thin air by magic. You <b>know</b> what a projector is like in the Supernal, actually you know it in detail. And the components of the projector are a direct derivation of this Supernal idea when materialized in the Fallen. Since you don't want a particular projector, the information in the Supernal Projector is sufficient.<br /> <br /> Now, the Supernal isn't the collection of all things that can be and it doesn't make your work for you in selecting information. The Supernal Projector isn't any projector you want, <i>it is the most perfect yet most basic</i> version of the very concept of a projector. Absolutely any detail you want to add to it you must provide yourself: the information must <i>always</i> come from somewhere. This conjured projector may have any appearance you can imagine because by imagining it you're providing information, but anything beyond that you'll need the proper Arcana and parameters to weave in the spell the ability to seek that information. Whenever there's no specific information the spell <b>will</b> default to the plain, conceptual Supernal Projector.<br /> <br /> Computers are a particular thing. What is the Idea of a Computer? I would personally ask for Reach to make a working computer with an OS with Matter alone. Why? Because The Supernal Computer is governed by Matter, but The Supernal Windows is governed by Forces, as it is pure data, but you certainly can have this data already written in the Matter without writing it yourself. In both cases, though, you need to know <b>both </b>as far as the Supernal goes. The fact you don't know the code of the OS or the components of the computer from a physical standpoint doesn't change that you actually knows both in the Supernal. If you didn't, you wouldn't be able to get them regardless.<br /> <br /> So, the <b>Imago</b> is how you put the information you have into the spell. It is first your actual hard knowledge of the Supernal Symbols of the thing you want to make. Then, the details you can imagine <i><b>to add their Symbols to your creation</b></i>, because even those are actually coming from somewhere in the Supernal. Finally, <i>if there is any piece of information you need, but don't have</i>, then you add <b>Spell effects</b> that seek this information somehow, with clear parameters and the proper Arcana for that effect.<br /> <br /> Without the proper information, no spell works. It so happens that this information isn't physical, but Supernal. Hence we saying in answer to the OP that for rules' sake it is magic, but from a lore standpoint it is actually a structured body of knowledge, even if one that doesn't exist IRL. The Mage that wants to give the properties of an Eel to a person with Life doesn't need to know enough biology to avoid mistakes because the spell does that, <b><i>but actually, in lore, what happens is that the Mage <u>already</u> knows more than enough Supernal Biology</i></b>. The Mage actually has the information needed, as long as they know what's an eel and what's a person, something <b>we </b>usually handwave for the sake of the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T20:25:25-08:00","id":1476141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476139#post1476139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why the Mage can create a projector with Matter. The Mage <b>knows</b> how the projector works <i>from a supernal perspective</i>. The Mage analysed projectors before with Mage Sight, or somehow learned how the <i>idea of a projector</i> is in details, so they can <i>picture the Supernal form of a projector exactly</i>.<br /> <br /> It is just as complete and elaborate as knowing the complete blueprint of a projector, actually even better. Then the Mage forms an Imago with <i>every single detail needed</i> for this idea, and brings the Supernal projector to the Fallen World. The fact the Mage doesn't know how the projector looks like inside in the Fallen World matters as much as an Astrophysicist not knowing how Neptune feels to the touch. It isn't the actual information that makes the actual thing be a thing.<br /> <br /> At no point information was created from thin air by magic. You <b>know</b> what a projector is like in the Supernal, actually you know it in detail. And the components of the projector are a direct derivation of this Supernal idea when materialized in the Fallen. Since you don't want a particular projector, the information in the Supernal Projector is sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out that &quot;know&quot; isn't quite the right word \u2014 as any number of frustrated Obrimos can recount, Gnosis is not a wholly conscious form of awareness, hence why the closest Phenomenal expressions of the Supernal outside of Emanations are in the deepest parts of the realms of the universal unconscious, archmasters' loyal subsouls drift out of fidelity toward their makers' plans as they get sidetracked by unspoken desires, and Paradox stems from fumbling the metaphysical legerdemain of spellcasting and grabbing the wrong symbol.<br /> <br /> You can have Crafts 0 and Science 0 and still create a small house with working lights and a generator because you know what lights and a generator are and that's enough to steer your Gnosis toward the right symbols to express your intent, because Gnosis and knowledge aren't quite the same thing \u2014 the emphasis in Awakened pedagogy on experiencing the Mysteries rather than simply being told about them is significant here, as is the fact that Yantras are most directly analogized to mnemonic aids.<br /> <br /> That is to say, you know what a projector looks like, and you form an Imago indicating what the end result you want looks like, and in reaching for symbols that produce that outcome, you tap into the subset of Projectorness you want to emanate into the Phenomenal World and would be hard-pressed to explain the contortions of spirit and exercises of enlightened will you engaged in without resorting to metaphor, because despite dealing with phenomena that are prosaically understandable, the way spellcasting works is not known so much as felt.<br /> <br /> You don't need to thoroughly scrutinize a projector to make one based on your recollection of those days in high school where the teacher turned off the lights and projected chemistry edutainment shorts from the 1970s onto the whiteboard, but the product of that spell will probably be a little revealing re: your unconscious ideas about projectors if you just let the magic fill in the blanks instead of specifying exactly what you need (to say nothing of what Paradox might do).<br /> <br /> tl;dr Magic is significantly involved with imagination and intuition and instinct, and while that doesn't preclude the involvement of knowledge it definitely doesn't require it in stricter terms than specifying toward your desired outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T20:26:06-08:00","id":1476142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476138#post1476138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Assuming for a moment that the thread is a sincere attempt to understand Awakening\u2019s metaphysics, could you perhaps explain what you are having difficulty accepting or understanding ? </div> </div> </div> </div>The sincerity, mostly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T20:34:28-08:00","id":1476144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476142#post1476142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sincerity, mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm\u2026wrong \u201cyou\u201d. Sorry. I meant that as a question for pcontop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T10:07:36-08:00","id":1476163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1476141#post1476141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out that &quot;know&quot; isn't quite the right word</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on how you define knowledge.<br /> <br /> In that case, I'm going for the concept of having the information, no matter how you understand or classify it in your head, how conscious your hold on it is or isn't. Intuitive knowledge isn't structured knowledge, but is still knowledge, and can even be a huge amount of knowledge even if the person knowing is incapable of parsing it to others in a meaningful way or understand how they know. In such a sense, the Mage knows.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of this conversation, Spells follow natural rules based on the information provided. The Mage's scientific understanding and capacity to explain it is immaterial to this fact. The same way that cooking follows the laws of physics and chemistry despite how the cook conceptualizes what they're doing, and a traditional folk treatment that actually works follow natural rules despite the healer understanding them or not, the healer knows how to get hold of a lot of information (fever, infection, infectious state of a wound, most can make moderately adequate prognosis from pus, swelling, feces, urine and other data, even if it is made out of intuitive information and backed by makeshift explanations).<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the Mage knows the information they need to put in the spell, or how to seek it, and the rolls and rules help define if there's an error in the result. So it comes from knowledge, even if intuitive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T10:45:48-08:00","id":1476165,"title":"","content":"I think the question of rebuilding a book from a fragment might emerge from the philosophical question of what a book actually is.<br /> <br /> I understand that a basic introductory philosophical query would be &quot;what is a chair/prove the chair exists&quot;, which I think contributes to the matter of how one might form imagos. I think even for mages, that's not quite a settled question; some say a chair is a thing in its own right, holistic and enclosed, some say it's merely a shape imposed on substance, some go more abstract and think that a chair emerges from the concepts it represents.<br /> <br /> So if you have a fragment of a book, it can be a question of whether or not it is approached in terms of being defined as merely part of a whole, where you possess the means to grasp the properties of its wholeness and fill it back in.<br /> <br /> For the creation of something entirely new, I'd still say it gets back into a matter of how the Supernal doesn't quite deal with certain specificities. An object that will come into existence with some of its incidental details filled in according to some general standard is one thing, while recreating a person's authorial voice or exploring a hypothetical of their mindset is more complex and narrow.<br /> <br /> I would say that's a reason to not really be able to recreate Hemmingway's mind on a foundation of nothing, but sometimes Awakened magic does deal with more esoteric subjects, and in cases like that it can require a base to work with. Supernal magic short of archmastery might not recreate a person ex nihilio, but I would say it can engage with some things that they leave behind on a level that can draw something out of them in order to create new instances of them. Mages are probably still going to debate whether or not the thing can ever be definitively regarded as an actual product of their particular artifice.<br /> <br /> But sure, any of this inquiry is useful only insofar as it might give one insight into some interesting edge cases for creative thaumaturgy or ideas for some of the Mysteries that the Awakened might pursue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-10-2022, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}